WEBVTT

1
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:21.625
Hey, man!

2
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.875
Don't go into the water!
It gets very deep.

3
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:31.875
Hey, uncle!

4
00:02:17.208 --> 00:02:19.458
MATRU MAYA

5
00:02:21.291 --> 00:02:23.541
Hey! Splash some water on your face.

6
00:02:31.708 --> 00:02:33.666
NANA NANI PARK

7
00:02:59.875 --> 00:03:01.791
Who delivers the paper in Matru Maya?

8
00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:03.500
What happened, uncle?

9
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.416
I do not want all these pamphlets

10
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.250
for coaching class, marriage,

11
00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:10.750
sarees for sweets,

12
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:14.375
for yoga this and that.

13
00:03:15.541 --> 00:03:16.916
I don't have a pen.

14
00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:23.916
Hey, man! Hey, man! Have you lost it?

15
00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:42.458
Why have you chained the chair?
Are you a cop now?

16
00:03:42.541 --> 00:03:45.208
Planning to trick the thieves?
Hey, don't be shy.

17
00:03:46.041 --> 00:03:47.541
- Hey!
- Hey!

18
00:04:09.208 --> 00:04:10.708
Oh, Mom!

19
00:04:20.958 --> 00:04:22.458
I went to pee, sir.

20
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:24.208
I have kidney stones.

21
00:04:24.291 --> 00:04:27.208
Doctor advised me to drink
barley water, beer, buttermilk.

22
00:04:27.291 --> 00:04:29.916
It helps the stone to disintegrate
and pass through urine.

23
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.583
I've got hemorrhoids too, sir.

24
00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:35.500
Doctor advised me to use western-style
toilet, so it's easier to pass stool.

25
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:39.541
I brought this chair, made a hole in it.
So, I could sit and poop comfortably.

26
00:04:39.625 --> 00:04:42.000
Some idiot took it away. What do I do?

27
00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:43.625
But I'm not going to give up.

28
00:04:43.708 --> 00:04:45.958
I brought another one,
and I've chained it.

29
00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:48.000
Let's see who dare steals it now.

30
00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:05.166
Uncle, a new strong beer is here.

31
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.541
Give it, brother. Here.

32
00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:11.750
Time to close shop, come on.

33
00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:13.541
- Pass this.
- Come on. Time's up.

34
00:05:22.458 --> 00:05:23.750
Hey, hey...

35
00:05:25.083 --> 00:05:26.125
- Good evening.
- Hello.

36
00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:27.791
- Focus on your work.
- Yes, sir.

37
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.125
- You are late today.
- Yes.

38
00:07:08.291 --> 00:07:11.208
- How are you?
- Hi... Nanhe.

39
00:07:11.541 --> 00:07:15.791
When your parents put you in school
to make you a doctor or engineer,

40
00:07:15.875 --> 00:07:18.041
you should have become one, you bastard!

41
00:07:18.541 --> 00:07:21.500
Why did you have to come
and make my life a living hell?

42
00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:25.458
I let you stay on the second floor
out of sheer kindness

43
00:07:25.541 --> 00:07:27.125
and you act like a king?

44
00:07:27.208 --> 00:07:30.958
I told you to get the stuff two days ago,
and you went today.

45
00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.750
That too, when it's busy.

46
00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:35.375
Oh, sir! There was too much work.

47
00:07:35.458 --> 00:07:38.666
Eid and Navratri are both
around the corner, so I wasn't free.

48
00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.291
So, will you speed up

49
00:07:40.375 --> 00:07:43.375
or will you wipe out the business,
you wretch?

50
00:07:43.458 --> 00:07:45.291
He was on the machine late last night.

51
00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:46.750
I even made his video.

52
00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:50.291
Move. Come on, move.
Your work is done. You have served tea.

53
00:07:50.375 --> 00:07:53.083
We have work to do,
and you keep messing around.

54
00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:55.500
What were you sewing last night?

55
00:07:59.375 --> 00:08:01.333
Nanhe! Come upstairs.

56
00:08:05.208 --> 00:08:06.541
Yes, ma'am.

57
00:08:06.625 --> 00:08:07.708
Hey, Nanhe.

58
00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.833
Why did you make this so loose?

59
00:08:10.916 --> 00:08:12.583
It fits perfectly, ma'am.

60
00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:14.541
What looks perfect?

61
00:08:14.625 --> 00:08:16.791
Look at how loose this is. Look.

62
00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:20.708
Then it will become very tight.
You will find it difficult to breathe.

63
00:08:20.791 --> 00:08:23.666
You said the same thing earlier too,
and spoiled my dress.

64
00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.791
A snug fit won't suit you.

65
00:08:26.666 --> 00:08:27.958
What did you say?

66
00:08:28.791 --> 00:08:32.833
If I make it any more tighter than this,
it will end up squeezing this matter.

67
00:08:32.916 --> 00:08:36.416
If it was a blouse, I would've sewn a cup,
but you don't want that.

68
00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.916
Everything gets adjusted in that style.

69
00:08:50.791 --> 00:08:53.375
This bloody fucker
was touching me inappropriately!

70
00:08:53.458 --> 00:08:56.250
- What?
- Sir, I was just explaining the fitting.

71
00:08:56.333 --> 00:09:00.458
Yeah, like you are some big designer,
trying to explain to me how it works.

72
00:09:00.541 --> 00:09:02.750
He refers to my body part as "matter".

73
00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:04.250
Why don't you tell me, sir?

74
00:09:04.333 --> 00:09:07.083
Does anybody refer
to a woman's body part as "matter"?

75
00:09:07.166 --> 00:09:08.083
No, no, no.

76
00:09:08.166 --> 00:09:10.916
- You referred to it as matter... matter.
- No, that's not...

77
00:09:11.791 --> 00:09:14.166
Please wait.
We have a long history. I mean...

78
00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.875
Sir, your time is over now.

79
00:09:16.958 --> 00:09:19.000
Will this petty guy tell me
how to live my life

80
00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:20.875
- and expect me to listen to him?
- No, no.

81
00:09:20.958 --> 00:09:23.833
And, you, if you have some self-respect,

82
00:09:23.916 --> 00:09:26.250
then don't ever
step foot in his shop again.

83
00:09:26.916 --> 00:09:27.916
Listen, please wait!

84
00:09:33.416 --> 00:09:34.875
What is she doing?

85
00:09:34.958 --> 00:09:36.625
- Taking a selfie.
- Shut up!

86
00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:39.125
I swear I'll make you
famous on social media,

87
00:09:39.208 --> 00:09:41.541
or I'll change my name, got it?

88
00:09:51.333 --> 00:09:52.958
This is not true, sir.

89
00:09:56.291 --> 00:09:57.583
Bloody bastard!

90
00:09:57.666 --> 00:09:59.666
Sir, I'm not the one at fault here.

91
00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:04.416
All the fault lies with God
who blessed a pervert like you

92
00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.958
with such talent.

93
00:10:06.375 --> 00:10:11.000
I'll make sure
that nobody employs you in our circle.

94
00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.416
<i>Know your future for just ten rupees.</i>

95
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:24.833
<i>Libras, your moons are not aligned.</i>

96
00:10:24.916 --> 00:10:27.333
<i>It seems like
you're in for a lot of trouble.</i>

97
00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:31.833
Hey. This says I'm under
the influence of malefic planets.

98
00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:35.125
Says that I'm going
to land in trouble soon.

99
00:10:35.708 --> 00:10:38.166
- Whatever will be, will be.
- Whatever will be, will be.

100
00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:41.833
Forget it, man!
Why should I pay to hear bad news?

101
00:10:42.833 --> 00:10:46.250
Fresh watermelon, fresh mangoes,
everything is fresh...

102
00:10:52.875 --> 00:10:54.833
Trouble!

103
00:11:11.791 --> 00:11:13.958
This city of Mumbai is a market.

104
00:11:14.041 --> 00:11:16.041
People start their lives fresh everyday.

105
00:11:16.125 --> 00:11:20.416
<i>Smell fresh and buy fresh.
And bid on fresh.</i>

106
00:11:20.875 --> 00:11:25.958
<i>And when it starts to smell,
they cut it, and throw it away.</i>

107
00:11:28.208 --> 00:11:29.541
Hello, sir. Any work...

108
00:11:29.625 --> 00:11:31.291
I beg of you, get lost.

109
00:11:31.375 --> 00:11:33.166
Nobody will give you
work in this market.

110
00:11:33.625 --> 00:11:36.500
You get out of here, there is no work
for you here. Go.

111
00:11:38.375 --> 00:11:40.250
Buddy, I feel that...

112
00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:42.916
Asshole, you've been feeling
for the last 100 years.

113
00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.958
I've been telling you,
"Nanhe, do something, step up."

114
00:11:48.083 --> 00:11:51.666
You were leaning on
Mr. Jumman for the last three years.

115
00:11:53.166 --> 00:11:56.750
Man, God has blessed you with talent.
Understand?

116
00:11:56.833 --> 00:11:58.500
And what is your head full of?

117
00:11:58.583 --> 00:11:59.958
Just shit. Bullshit!

118
00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:01.916
Here, have some.

119
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.791
If you want to succeed,
open your own shop, Nanhe.

120
00:12:25.958 --> 00:12:27.416
Please turn off the AC.

121
00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:28.500
Yes, madam.

122
00:12:39.583 --> 00:12:44.083
Now, everything is quiet here, ma'am.
Builders have put up their board outside.

123
00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:48.166
Hey! You didn't even water my plants?

124
00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.416
I was on leave for ten days, ma'am.

125
00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:55.208
Whoever moves out,
leaves their pots and plants here.

126
00:12:55.291 --> 00:12:56.708
They just wither away here.

127
00:12:56.791 --> 00:12:59.458
I've given away so many, ma'am,
to so many people.

128
00:12:59.541 --> 00:13:00.875
How long will you be staying?

129
00:13:00.958 --> 00:13:03.500
- I will stay here itself now.
- Ma'am.

130
00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:06.500
Mr. Jayanti, the broker,
was bothering me a lot,

131
00:13:06.583 --> 00:13:08.958
so I gave him
Mr. Randheer's U.S. contact number.

132
00:13:09.041 --> 00:13:10.041
Why did you do that?

133
00:13:10.125 --> 00:13:12.833
Don't you dare
share his number without asking me.

134
00:13:12.916 --> 00:13:15.083
- And you stay away from this mess.
- Okay, ma'am.

135
00:13:15.166 --> 00:13:16.166
Go.

136
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.500
May God bless!

137
00:13:59.041 --> 00:14:00.208
Hey, Nanhe.

138
00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.791
- Bilkis ma'am.
- Hey, no need! How are you?

139
00:14:03.875 --> 00:14:05.625
I'm good, how are you Bilkis ma'am?

140
00:14:05.708 --> 00:14:08.875
I'm not Bilkis anymore, I'm Bimla now.
Changed name after marriage.

141
00:14:08.958 --> 00:14:10.458
So you're a Hindu now?

142
00:14:10.541 --> 00:14:12.208
Yeah, I have the freedom.

143
00:14:12.291 --> 00:14:15.166
Do you remember Mr. Sonu?
The ferocious tomcat.

144
00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.166
The fat, tall, wide, black bull.

145
00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.833
- Sonu Gadhwali Production?
- He's my husband.

146
00:14:19.916 --> 00:14:22.583
- I have left Saroj's dance group.
- I see.

147
00:14:22.666 --> 00:14:25.958
I've started my own production
of Bhojpuri movies, independently.

148
00:14:26.083 --> 00:14:28.458
- Okay.
- Forget about me, how are you doing?

149
00:14:28.541 --> 00:14:31.291
- Not so good.
- "Not so good." Hold this.

150
00:14:33.916 --> 00:14:35.708
You are my old champion.

151
00:14:36.875 --> 00:14:38.125
- This is my number.
- Okay.

152
00:14:38.208 --> 00:14:41.500
I do a lot of shows
in the Dubai, Riyadh, Oman, Muscat region.

153
00:14:41.583 --> 00:14:43.416
I take the whole Bollywood theme there.

154
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.666
I get big orders for my Bollywood themes.

155
00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.541
You do have the sewing set up, right?

156
00:14:49.583 --> 00:14:51.500
- Yeah, I do.
- Sure?

157
00:14:51.583 --> 00:14:53.458
Look, I don't want to take any risk.

158
00:14:53.541 --> 00:14:57.041
No, I have it.
I have a machine, bench and a place.

159
00:14:57.666 --> 00:14:59.708
- Okay, buzz me.
- What?

160
00:15:00.416 --> 00:15:02.166
- Call me, call!
- Okay.

161
00:15:06.041 --> 00:15:09.500
Oh, God, you heard my prayers.
Thank you, thank you, dear God.

162
00:15:12.666 --> 00:15:15.958
Sewing machine for 15,000
and 5,000 for the place.

163
00:15:16.041 --> 00:15:18.625
Thread, bobbin and other stuff for 2,000.

164
00:15:18.708 --> 00:15:20.666
Table and chair for 4,000.

165
00:15:21.333 --> 00:15:24.958
If you take some place on rent,
it'll be around 15,000,

166
00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:27.750
and a deposit of 50,000.

167
00:15:27.833 --> 00:15:31.208
If you add the electricity bill,
then it will be 2,000 more.

168
00:15:31.291 --> 00:15:33.375
It'll come to around 100,000 rupees.

169
00:15:33.875 --> 00:15:35.291
Do you have any savings?

170
00:15:36.333 --> 00:15:39.583
- Yeah. I have some savings.
- Okay.

171
00:15:39.666 --> 00:15:43.750
Do one thing, Nanhe.
Do not say no to any work.

172
00:15:43.833 --> 00:15:44.875
Okay.

173
00:15:44.958 --> 00:15:49.208
Right? Like security, or walking dogs.

174
00:15:49.291 --> 00:15:52.333
Right? Loading, painting,
whatever you can get hold of.

175
00:15:52.416 --> 00:15:54.125
Save your earnings.

176
00:15:55.125 --> 00:15:58.125
Baburam, if I could get a place
to set up my business

177
00:15:58.208 --> 00:16:03.333
and some tailoring work,
then my practice wouldn't suffer.

178
00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.750
You shouldn't have bragged about
your talent to Sana.

179
00:16:06.833 --> 00:16:11.333
Think before you speak
and look before you leap.

180
00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.416
<i>Hey, these penniless ponies chase after me</i>

181
00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.333
<i>Token in hand
They've stood in a queue for eternity</i>

182
00:16:36.208 --> 00:16:38.541
Stand straight. Stand straight. Yes.

183
00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.583
Is this the way to dance?

184
00:16:43.291 --> 00:16:44.291
Like this...

185
00:16:44.333 --> 00:16:47.958
<i>These penniless ponies chase after me</i>

186
00:16:48.416 --> 00:16:50.041
And all these scowling faces.

187
00:16:51.291 --> 00:16:53.333
Why are you laughing? Go, take a break!

188
00:16:56.125 --> 00:16:57.541
Yes, Kuku.

189
00:16:57.625 --> 00:16:58.958
Yes, Kuku.

190
00:16:59.708 --> 00:17:01.333
Yes, yes. Passports are ready.

191
00:17:01.416 --> 00:17:03.583
- Do you eat chicken?
- Yes.

192
00:17:03.666 --> 00:17:05.458
- Kavita, give him the pizza.
- Yes, ma'am.

193
00:17:07.958 --> 00:17:10.500
Here, this is the sample.
The order is of 200,000.

194
00:17:11.083 --> 00:17:12.625
- 200,000?
- Hand it over to him.

195
00:17:16.708 --> 00:17:17.958
It will be done.

196
00:17:18.041 --> 00:17:20.375
All your dancers
have almost the same figures,

197
00:17:20.458 --> 00:17:21.708
so it will not take too long.

198
00:17:24.833 --> 00:17:26.083
You are very smart.

199
00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:31.625
This is one lot,
there are two more groups, 90 in all.

200
00:17:31.708 --> 00:17:33.500
I'll manage. When do we start?

201
00:17:33.583 --> 00:17:35.208
It has started, boss.

202
00:17:35.291 --> 00:17:37.666
- I need everything ready in two weeks.
- Two weeks?

203
00:17:38.833 --> 00:17:42.500
If you cannot do it, better speak up now.
Do not hum and haw later.

204
00:17:42.875 --> 00:17:44.000
Salim is ready.

205
00:17:45.708 --> 00:17:46.708
It will be done.

206
00:17:46.791 --> 00:17:47.958
You keep this for now.

207
00:17:48.041 --> 00:17:49.375
Give it to him.

208
00:17:50.958 --> 00:17:51.958
Now get to work.

209
00:18:03.291 --> 00:18:05.125
Welcome, Nanhe, greetings.

210
00:18:05.208 --> 00:18:07.000
Hello. I want this cloth.

211
00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.000
This golden one.

212
00:18:09.083 --> 00:18:11.291
Hey, Chagan.
Get the golden stuff from the corner.

213
00:18:11.375 --> 00:18:12.375
I'll get it.

214
00:19:44.416 --> 00:19:47.916
- Bablu pooped, right?
- Yes, Bablu pooped.

215
00:19:48.708 --> 00:19:50.125
I'll confirm about tomorrow later.

216
00:19:50.208 --> 00:19:52.666
My baby, sweetheart, cutie pie...

217
00:20:33.541 --> 00:20:35.250
Here, 10,000 rupees.

218
00:20:35.333 --> 00:20:37.541
Give me 50,000 at least.

219
00:20:37.625 --> 00:20:40.625
Are you crazy?
I don't print notes at my home.

220
00:20:40.708 --> 00:20:42.083
I'll get advance, I'll pay you.

221
00:20:42.166 --> 00:20:44.791
You have a shop,
when will you start rolling?

222
00:20:45.125 --> 00:20:47.875
See, if you cannot do it, better speak up.

223
00:20:47.958 --> 00:20:50.833
- I'll get it done from Salim this time.
- No, ma'am. I'll do it.

224
00:20:50.916 --> 00:20:52.041
Go, now get moving.

225
00:20:54.208 --> 00:20:55.666
Oh, Sonu sir!

226
00:20:57.041 --> 00:20:58.791
Not that way.

227
00:21:11.166 --> 00:21:13.375
Hey, asshole, move!

228
00:21:16.916 --> 00:21:18.583
You're working out of my shop?

229
00:21:18.666 --> 00:21:19.958
Hey, catch him, catch him!

230
00:21:20.041 --> 00:21:21.208
Don't let him get away!

231
00:21:38.833 --> 00:21:41.041
I don't like eggs in the morning.

232
00:21:41.125 --> 00:21:42.875
- Slow down.
- Omelet and all.

233
00:21:43.875 --> 00:21:46.208
He won't do anything. Hey, come here.

234
00:21:49.791 --> 00:21:50.958
That's cool!

235
00:21:51.708 --> 00:21:53.916
His poop is solid like a donut.

236
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.375
This idiot poops
mashed potatoes with gravy.

237
00:21:57.541 --> 00:21:59.708
- This dog really glows.
- Yeah.

238
00:21:59.791 --> 00:22:01.625
Ma'am uses some cream.

239
00:22:01.708 --> 00:22:04.291
Ma'am uses the cream
and he is the one that glows.

240
00:22:05.708 --> 00:22:08.476
You know, that woman who stays behind,
in Rashi Towers? Always fully decked up.

241
00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:11.250
- That Sasural Simple girl?
- Yeah.

242
00:22:11.333 --> 00:22:14.291
The other day she was walking
her dog, wearing a gold chain,

243
00:22:14.375 --> 00:22:15.666
right here behind the park.

244
00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.666
Someone came from behind,
snatched the chain and ran away.

245
00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:20.458
Everything happened in a jiffy.

246
00:22:20.541 --> 00:22:23.958
There was a theft here as well
the night before last, did you know?

247
00:22:24.041 --> 00:22:28.083
That old man in the park,
who moved around with a walker.

248
00:22:28.166 --> 00:22:29.958
<i>His kids live abroad.</i>

249
00:22:30.041 --> 00:22:33.000
<i>Lonely old people are very easy targets.</i>

250
00:22:33.083 --> 00:22:34.541
<i>So, these petty thieves</i>

251
00:22:34.625 --> 00:22:37.916
<i>manage to get into the house
by hook or by crook,</i>

252
00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.083
<i>and steal around
30,000-40,000 very easily.</i>

253
00:22:41.166 --> 00:22:44.833
<i>What can the cops do?
They can't keep an eye on every oldie.</i>

254
00:22:44.916 --> 00:22:48.583
And who else has the time
to go around doing social work.

255
00:23:06.833 --> 00:23:08.708
Come on now, time is up. Get going!

256
00:23:08.791 --> 00:23:09.875
Here, hold this.

257
00:23:15.125 --> 00:23:16.750
- Sir, your parcel.
- Yes.

258
00:23:32.333 --> 00:23:33.958
- Hello, sir.
- Focus on your work.

259
00:23:39.416 --> 00:23:40.458
You can take yours.

260
00:23:40.541 --> 00:23:43.958
And I want my tea in the morning on time.
Hey! Hey!

261
00:24:52.458 --> 00:24:55.416
Let me go! I am sorry!

262
00:24:55.500 --> 00:24:56.833
I am sorry!

263
00:24:56.916 --> 00:24:58.708
Hey, I am sorry! Forgive me, sir.

264
00:24:58.791 --> 00:25:00.958
Sir, I swear on my mother,
it was a mistake.

265
00:25:01.041 --> 00:25:04.541
I won't do it again, never again, sir,
please let me go.

266
00:25:05.333 --> 00:25:08.583
Let me go, sir.
I swear I won't do it again.

267
00:25:08.666 --> 00:25:10.416
Let me go.

268
00:25:10.500 --> 00:25:12.791
I am a very poor man.
I won't do it again.

269
00:25:12.875 --> 00:25:13.875
Let me go.

270
00:25:27.125 --> 00:25:30.750
You... kill me.

271
00:25:32.041 --> 00:25:33.458
You want money?

272
00:25:34.041 --> 00:25:39.708
You want jewelry?
I don't want to live. Kill me.

273
00:25:39.791 --> 00:25:41.583
- Strangle me to death!
- No, sir!

274
00:25:41.666 --> 00:25:42.708
- Kill me!
- No, sir!

275
00:25:42.791 --> 00:25:46.083
- No, sir! Let me go, sir. No!
- Kill me please!

276
00:25:51.625 --> 00:25:53.375
- Help Me.
- Let me go.

277
00:25:53.458 --> 00:25:54.750
I made a mistake, sir.

278
00:25:54.833 --> 00:25:57.208
- Let me go, sir!
- Please, help me.

279
00:25:57.291 --> 00:26:00.833
- Let me go!
- Please, please help me.

280
00:26:42.250 --> 00:26:45.666
My shop is like a Rajdhani coupe.
I'll get it done at a cheap rate.

281
00:26:46.250 --> 00:26:47.291
Yeah, that's fine.

282
00:26:48.750 --> 00:26:51.041
Should I shift
this copper to the warehouse?

283
00:26:51.125 --> 00:26:54.916
No, let it be. He is a tailor.
This is of no use to him.

284
00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:58.083
Yeah, yeah. Okay. It's fine. Let it be.

285
00:26:58.166 --> 00:26:59.166
- Okay?
- Yes.

286
00:27:01.250 --> 00:27:03.708
Baburam, how long
will you work as a hawker?

287
00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.125
You should set up something big.

288
00:27:06.208 --> 00:27:08.833
- I'll arrange it for you.
- I'll pay you the advance.

289
00:27:08.916 --> 00:27:09.958
Okay. Okay.

290
00:27:10.041 --> 00:27:12.375
Hey, tailor.
Are you here to buy the place?

291
00:27:12.458 --> 00:27:13.583
Tailor.

292
00:27:17.500 --> 00:27:19.291
- How much is it?
- Sixty thousand.

293
00:27:19.375 --> 00:27:20.625
- What?
- Sixty thousand.

294
00:27:22.208 --> 00:27:23.750
Did you not tell him?

295
00:27:23.833 --> 00:27:25.708
Rent is 20,000, and 100,000 deposit.

296
00:27:25.791 --> 00:27:28.666
Brother Liyakat, once his work picks up,
he will pay you.

297
00:27:28.750 --> 00:27:30.958
Trust me. I am here. He is one of our own.

298
00:27:32.166 --> 00:27:35.000
There is a room upstairs as well.
Go, take a look.

299
00:27:35.083 --> 00:27:36.250
- A room!
- Okay.

300
00:27:50.708 --> 00:27:52.125
Hey, Baburam!

301
00:27:52.208 --> 00:27:54.041
This is...

302
00:27:57.250 --> 00:28:00.416
Hey, Phoolan.
There is a smell coming from Kamath's.

303
00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:01.750
What kind of smell?

304
00:28:03.916 --> 00:28:05.250
Like something rotten.

305
00:28:11.125 --> 00:28:12.708
Climb slowly, be careful.

306
00:28:32.541 --> 00:28:33.750
The old man is alive.

307
00:28:33.833 --> 00:28:35.333
What? He's alive?

308
00:28:35.416 --> 00:28:37.583
Come on, splash some water.

309
00:28:39.958 --> 00:28:41.958
Easy, easy, sir.

310
00:28:44.791 --> 00:28:46.125
Here, have some water.

311
00:28:51.708 --> 00:28:54.083
- Sir, are you okay?
- Sir, your glasses.

312
00:28:55.083 --> 00:28:56.083
Yes.

313
00:28:57.333 --> 00:28:59.625
You're badly hurt.
Should we go to the hospital?

314
00:28:59.708 --> 00:29:02.500
<i>There has been a robbery,
but the old man is alive.</i>

315
00:29:02.583 --> 00:29:03.833
<i>There were three dead rats.</i>

316
00:29:03.916 --> 00:29:09.875
Nowadays you get that pack,
that rat trap with the glue. Yeah.

317
00:29:09.958 --> 00:29:11.333
We thought the old man had died.

318
00:29:11.416 --> 00:29:12.416
Hey, watchman!

319
00:29:13.041 --> 00:29:15.166
Idiot. What are you looking at? Come here.

320
00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:16.750
Yes, sir.

321
00:29:17.791 --> 00:29:19.125
Is this how you do your duty?

322
00:29:24.125 --> 00:29:26.875
It stinks so bad.
Wonder how many rats have died.

323
00:29:27.250 --> 00:29:29.708
- Hey, watchman, put in the box.
- Sir, it is glued.

324
00:29:29.833 --> 00:29:33.250
<i>Do you people have any shame or not?</i>

325
00:29:33.333 --> 00:29:36.791
<i>An old man lives here alone.
You should take care of him.</i>

326
00:29:37.416 --> 00:29:41.166
Had he been dead
and his body were rotting for four days,

327
00:29:43.041 --> 00:29:45.666
would you have come to pick it up?

328
00:30:26.833 --> 00:30:28.291
Here, sir! Come.

329
00:30:30.583 --> 00:30:31.583
What all was taken?

330
00:30:32.250 --> 00:30:34.875
Two silver idols were stolen.

331
00:30:35.625 --> 00:30:38.750
My wife's
gold wedding necklace was stolen,

332
00:30:38.833 --> 00:30:42.166
and my savings of 1,200 rupees were taken.

333
00:30:42.250 --> 00:30:43.250
Twelve hundred...

334
00:30:43.291 --> 00:30:44.351
<i>Live like a king,
eat, drink and make merry</i>

335
00:30:44.375 --> 00:30:45.375
Hey, turn off the music.

336
00:30:45.458 --> 00:30:49.125
- Don't be afraid. Will you get me biryani?
- I will do break dance too. Wait!

337
00:30:49.208 --> 00:30:50.333
Do an exotic dance too.

338
00:30:50.416 --> 00:30:52.208
Would you like lamb or chicken?

339
00:30:52.291 --> 00:30:55.333
- Lamb. Ask sir as well.
- Sir?

340
00:30:55.666 --> 00:30:56.875
- Sir?
- Yeah?

341
00:30:56.958 --> 00:30:58.166
- Something to eat?
- No.

342
00:30:58.250 --> 00:31:00.375
- No, no.
- Lamb, lamb.

343
00:31:00.458 --> 00:31:03.083
Sir must have had breakfast at home.

344
00:31:03.166 --> 00:31:04.875
Sir lives all by himself.

345
00:31:05.416 --> 00:31:07.041
That's why there was a robbery.

346
00:31:07.583 --> 00:31:10.250
- Found unconscious on the floor, alone.
- By himself?

347
00:31:10.333 --> 00:31:12.708
The robber stole
some cheap stuff and ran off.

348
00:31:12.791 --> 00:31:16.000
- My wife's wedding necklace is cheap?
- Emotional attachment for you.

349
00:31:16.083 --> 00:31:19.666
Hit sir in the face and ran away.
Sir was drunk at that time.

350
00:31:19.750 --> 00:31:22.041
I had beer and dozed off.

351
00:31:22.125 --> 00:31:25.875
Drinking beer and being drunk
is one and the same thing, sir.

352
00:31:25.958 --> 00:31:29.208
Hit you in the face, but you didn't
see him. That's why you're alive.

353
00:31:29.291 --> 00:31:30.416
No, I did see him!

354
00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:34.166
I did see him.

355
00:31:34.250 --> 00:31:36.333
- Can you recognize him?
- Yes, I can.

356
00:31:36.416 --> 00:31:38.500
Then he must be a newbie.

357
00:31:38.583 --> 00:31:40.750
You know, in our criminal community,

358
00:31:40.833 --> 00:31:44.666
if the victim sees your face,
then you have to kill the victim.

359
00:31:44.791 --> 00:31:47.625
Who wants to deal with
the whole eye-witness trouble later on.

360
00:31:50.791 --> 00:31:54.375
- What has he stolen?
- He's not an ordinary thief.

361
00:31:54.458 --> 00:31:57.333
He supplied 40 SUVs in the elections.

362
00:31:57.416 --> 00:32:00.625
- To whom?
- Who uses cars in elections?

363
00:32:00.708 --> 00:32:01.708
Exactly.

364
00:32:09.500 --> 00:32:12.625
Sir, last year we found 16 bodies.

365
00:32:12.708 --> 00:32:15.583
That too after a gap of four to six days.

366
00:32:15.666 --> 00:32:18.250
We got to know
only when the stench started spreading.

367
00:32:18.333 --> 00:32:22.333
Do you get it?
Juhu, Malabar Hill, all posh areas.

368
00:32:22.416 --> 00:32:24.708
So, be a little careful.

369
00:32:26.375 --> 00:32:28.166
After my wife passed away,

370
00:32:29.875 --> 00:32:33.750
people kept on bringing milk, curd, sugar,
cake for a couple of months.

371
00:32:33.833 --> 00:32:35.708
After that? It's been 12 years,

372
00:32:35.791 --> 00:32:38.708
and nobody has bothered
to ring the doorbell since.

373
00:32:38.791 --> 00:32:40.041
Not even me.

374
00:32:41.125 --> 00:32:45.875
Had my body been found today,
everybody would've come with flowers.

375
00:32:46.333 --> 00:32:47.708
Do you go to parks or not?

376
00:32:48.250 --> 00:32:50.125
Are you part of some group there?

377
00:32:50.791 --> 00:32:54.750
The thing is
you elderly people should

378
00:32:54.833 --> 00:32:56.291
be a little careful.

379
00:32:56.375 --> 00:32:59.916
So, start interacting with your neighbors.

380
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:04.250
When they will see you face to face,
they will realize that you exist.

381
00:33:04.833 --> 00:33:06.250
I am not that social.

382
00:33:06.333 --> 00:33:07.916
Okay. Then, become social.

383
00:33:35.666 --> 00:33:38.625
Come, come, come here!

384
00:33:38.708 --> 00:33:40.708
With water or without?

385
00:33:51.166 --> 00:33:53.708
There are so many people everywhere.

386
00:33:55.000 --> 00:33:58.625
Even amidst so many people,
a lonesome person is still lonely.

387
00:34:02.541 --> 00:34:03.541
Do you live alone?

388
00:34:05.875 --> 00:34:08.875
I am alone, and lonely...

389
00:34:09.416 --> 00:34:11.708
and getting older.

390
00:34:15.041 --> 00:34:18.041
I think one should not
install tiles in the washrooms.

391
00:34:19.708 --> 00:34:23.250
Old people tend to slip on tiles
and break their hips.

392
00:34:24.500 --> 00:34:28.000
And then, their body is found
after four days.

393
00:34:28.333 --> 00:34:31.000
- Whose body?
- Your body.

394
00:34:32.375 --> 00:34:36.500
My body.
His body, their body, everybody's body.

395
00:34:36.583 --> 00:34:38.500
Which is only found after the stench.

396
00:34:41.666 --> 00:34:44.458
- I was telling him...
- Does anybody

397
00:34:44.541 --> 00:34:48.708
talk about broken hips
and dead bodies at this age?

398
00:34:49.875 --> 00:34:52.375
You don't have tiles
in your washroom, do you?

399
00:34:57.583 --> 00:35:00.291
Dad, why do you have
to listen to anybody's lecture?

400
00:35:00.375 --> 00:35:02.041
- But...
- You should have walked away.

401
00:35:05.666 --> 00:35:08.416
Does this park allow purebred dogs only?

402
00:35:08.541 --> 00:35:11.458
- Ma'am, they are all stray dogs.
- They are strays?

403
00:35:11.541 --> 00:35:13.625
What are you, a millionaire?

404
00:35:13.708 --> 00:35:17.000
I'll get them vaccinated for rabies,
what will you do?

405
00:35:17.083 --> 00:35:20.000
Ma'am, then you might as well
talk to the park trustees.

406
00:35:20.083 --> 00:35:23.458
Really? I might as well
talk to the prime minister.

407
00:35:25.583 --> 00:35:29.583
And don't you dare
hit them in the future. Got it?

408
00:35:29.666 --> 00:35:31.208
I am a Punjabi. Punjabi.

409
00:35:31.291 --> 00:35:35.041
I'll make mincemeat out of you
and feed it to them. Bloody fucker!

410
00:35:41.500 --> 00:35:43.166
Hello.

411
00:35:43.250 --> 00:35:45.000
- Hello, ma'am.
- What is it?

412
00:35:47.041 --> 00:35:49.666
Your... Your handkerchief fell down there.

413
00:36:31.208 --> 00:36:32.416
You've done it!

414
00:36:32.500 --> 00:36:34.083
I'm making the full payment.

415
00:36:37.250 --> 00:36:38.250
Here.

416
00:36:40.541 --> 00:36:43.458
- Will you do a big project?
- Yeah, sure.

417
00:36:46.041 --> 00:36:48.583
Take a look.
You have two weeks, what do you say?

418
00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:53.083
- How much is the order for?
- 800,000.

419
00:36:55.458 --> 00:36:57.375
Tell me, or else I'll go to Salim.

420
00:36:57.458 --> 00:37:00.208
No, I'll do it.
I'll get a couple of more tailors.

421
00:37:00.291 --> 00:37:01.166
Right, Mushtaq?

422
00:37:01.250 --> 00:37:02.500
- We will work it out.
- Yes.

423
00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:07.875
One lakh rupees advance.

424
00:37:21.916 --> 00:37:25.333
These film industry guys
take people for a ride.

425
00:37:25.416 --> 00:37:26.583
Be careful, Nanhe.

426
00:37:26.666 --> 00:37:31.333
That's my Bilkis ma'am.
I have done a lot of work with her.

427
00:37:31.416 --> 00:37:32.875
She is honest to the core.

428
00:37:32.958 --> 00:37:34.708
The order is worth 800,000. Get it?

429
00:37:34.791 --> 00:37:35.708
What?

430
00:37:35.791 --> 00:37:38.500
Yeah, exactly.
They take people for a ride

431
00:37:38.583 --> 00:37:39.875
with their sweet talk.

432
00:37:39.958 --> 00:37:43.541
If tomorrow, Bilkis gives a flying kiss
and vanishes, what will you do?

433
00:37:43.625 --> 00:37:48.125
The rent for Liyakat's shop
and 700,000 extra, think about it, Nanhe.

434
00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:55.500
- You'll pay by card or cash?
- Cash.

435
00:37:59.833 --> 00:38:01.416
- Congratulations.
- Okay.

436
00:38:34.583 --> 00:38:37.000
Hey! What are you doing, man?

437
00:38:46.333 --> 00:38:48.333
Hey, Rondu, get me a juice.

438
00:38:48.416 --> 00:38:50.375
You'll have to wait, I have customers.

439
00:38:50.458 --> 00:38:52.916
- I don't look like a customer to you!
- Okay.

440
00:38:54.458 --> 00:38:55.541
You can take this.

441
00:38:58.416 --> 00:39:00.000
Why are you giving it for free?

442
00:39:01.583 --> 00:39:03.583
Take it. I've already had one.

443
00:39:07.125 --> 00:39:08.333
Are you new to Mumbai?

444
00:39:08.875 --> 00:39:11.250
- No, it's been three years.
- Three?

445
00:39:11.333 --> 00:39:13.666
Come on!
If he is offering, take it, Rawas.

446
00:39:13.916 --> 00:39:16.750
Why do you care about how
long he has been here?

447
00:39:20.583 --> 00:39:21.833
Add some ice.

448
00:39:22.583 --> 00:39:24.750
- Started your tantrums?
- It's really hot.

449
00:39:24.833 --> 00:39:27.500
Your heat is different, Rawas.
Ice won't be able to help you.

450
00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:34.833
I am thinking of moving to Dubai.

451
00:39:35.291 --> 00:39:40.541
The Arabs out there hide gold biscuits
in their nighties, Rondu.

452
00:39:41.333 --> 00:39:42.916
Yeah, they hide snakes in there too.

453
00:39:45.791 --> 00:39:48.083
Nighties are for ladies. Ladies.

454
00:39:48.166 --> 00:39:49.541
Who got laid?

455
00:39:49.625 --> 00:39:52.875
No. For the ladies. For women.

456
00:39:53.416 --> 00:39:55.458
The Arabs wear kaftans.

457
00:39:55.541 --> 00:39:57.166
Are you from Dubai?

458
00:39:57.583 --> 00:40:01.416
No, I am a tailor. I have sewn kaftans.

459
00:40:16.625 --> 00:40:17.625
Hey...

460
00:40:22.708 --> 00:40:25.291
Sir, there was a box here. Did you see it?

461
00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:29.791
I kept a box, big box here.
Did you not see it?

462
00:40:31.125 --> 00:40:34.750
My... I kept the machine right here,
did you not see it?

463
00:40:34.833 --> 00:40:37.333
Do you guys have eyes or not? Move!

464
00:40:38.208 --> 00:40:40.416
I had kept the machine right here, man.

465
00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:42.250
I kept the machine.

466
00:40:51.083 --> 00:40:52.125
Pakiya took it.

467
00:41:07.083 --> 00:41:10.416
Oh, my box! My box!

468
00:41:10.875 --> 00:41:14.416
- Yeah, what happened?
- Did you steal a box from Rondu stall?

469
00:41:16.791 --> 00:41:17.916
Bring it back.

470
00:41:18.750 --> 00:41:20.416
Oh, man!

471
00:41:21.750 --> 00:41:24.125
It was right here.
Right here, the machine...

472
00:41:37.041 --> 00:41:38.166
Come.

473
00:41:38.750 --> 00:41:41.708
- That guy won't beat me, right?
- Not at all, man.

474
00:41:41.791 --> 00:41:44.375
You come here. What's in the box?

475
00:41:44.458 --> 00:41:45.916
It's a sewing machine.

476
00:41:47.541 --> 00:41:49.583
- Who the fuck are you, man?
- Nanhe.

477
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:51.833
Fucker, I wanna know your job, not name.

478
00:41:51.916 --> 00:41:53.291
I am a women's tailor.

479
00:41:53.916 --> 00:41:55.041
Oh, yes.

480
00:41:55.125 --> 00:41:57.166
You mentioned. You sew Afghans, right?

481
00:41:57.750 --> 00:41:59.125
No, no. Not Afghans, kaftan.

482
00:42:01.333 --> 00:42:03.416
You're gonna rot here in Mumbai.

483
00:42:52.583 --> 00:42:53.583
Hey, tailor!

484
00:42:55.875 --> 00:42:58.333
- Where is your kid?
- He is at school.

485
00:43:06.416 --> 00:43:07.833
Do you want some breakfast?

486
00:43:08.958 --> 00:43:10.291
Will you get me Pav Bhaji?

487
00:43:32.416 --> 00:43:33.791
You are not dark-skinned.

488
00:43:34.458 --> 00:43:36.375
We apply shoe polish on our bodies.

489
00:43:38.041 --> 00:43:40.541
The work we do is a facade.

490
00:43:40.958 --> 00:43:44.375
Nobody cares whether
you're really disabled or faking it.

491
00:43:44.458 --> 00:43:45.875
If they are in a good mood,

492
00:43:45.958 --> 00:43:48.625
they will roll down the car window
and give money.

493
00:44:55.000 --> 00:44:56.666
Do I look like a beggar to you, fucker?

494
00:44:58.083 --> 00:45:02.041
If I slap you in front of everybody,
you'll lose all your respect.

495
00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:04.291
I'll pay you, sir.

496
00:45:04.375 --> 00:45:07.458
Things are working out slowly
and gradually, there's no issue now.

497
00:45:07.541 --> 00:45:10.041
I'll squeeze the money out of you.

498
00:45:10.125 --> 00:45:12.958
- Don't you take me lightly.
- Not at all.

499
00:45:13.041 --> 00:45:14.125
Got it?

500
00:45:17.541 --> 00:45:18.833
What is this?

501
00:45:20.125 --> 00:45:21.416
Sorry, brother.

502
00:45:25.458 --> 00:45:27.416
<i>Fresh, fresh. The mangoes are fresh.</i>

503
00:45:27.500 --> 00:45:29.375
POPRITER - BABURAM
FRUIT AND KAATE

504
00:45:29.458 --> 00:45:31.666
Fresh, fresh.

505
00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:34.625
- Everything is fresh?
- Of course.

506
00:45:34.708 --> 00:45:36.958
- Do you do home delivery?
- Where, ma'am?

507
00:45:37.041 --> 00:45:39.875
- Dhavalgiri, N.G. Road.
- It'll be done.

508
00:45:39.958 --> 00:45:42.250
Mrs. Handa, 201.
Do you want to write it down?

509
00:45:42.333 --> 00:45:45.458
- I'll remember.
- Mrs. Handa, 201, Dhavalgiri, N.G. Road.

510
00:45:45.541 --> 00:45:46.791
- Got it.
- Okay?

511
00:45:47.083 --> 00:45:49.000
I haven't seen you around here, ma'am.

512
00:45:49.458 --> 00:45:51.416
I've just came back from Canada.

513
00:45:51.500 --> 00:45:52.833
- From Canada? Yes.
- Yeah.

514
00:45:52.916 --> 00:45:54.166
- Send it over, okay?
- Yes.

515
00:45:54.916 --> 00:45:56.541
Dhavalgiri, one-zero...

516
00:46:00.041 --> 00:46:01.666
Hey, Nanhe. Thank you.

517
00:46:53.416 --> 00:46:55.208
Hey, wait, Premkanta!

518
00:46:55.291 --> 00:46:57.083
Hey, how are you?

519
00:46:57.166 --> 00:47:01.791
Invite us to Canada sometime, dear.
Let us taste the fun too.

520
00:47:01.875 --> 00:47:04.333
It's your own house,
you can come whenever you want.

521
00:47:04.416 --> 00:47:06.000
Randheer didn't come?

522
00:47:06.083 --> 00:47:09.583
He works around the clock.
He's always busy.

523
00:47:09.666 --> 00:47:11.958
And Satnaam is busier than him.

524
00:47:12.041 --> 00:47:13.333
Both of them work.

525
00:47:14.833 --> 00:47:18.208
Just that I miss Leela a lot.

526
00:47:20.541 --> 00:47:24.083
Hey, do call me whenever
you have religious or social gatherings.

527
00:47:24.166 --> 00:47:28.083
Very few turn up nowadays.
Everybody is busy in their own worlds.

528
00:47:28.166 --> 00:47:31.708
Look at Prem.
I'm seeing her after two months.

529
00:47:31.791 --> 00:47:33.708
You might as well meet us here only.

530
00:47:34.541 --> 00:47:35.916
Yeah, okay.

531
00:47:36.000 --> 00:47:40.500
I'll be right back.
I gotta say goodbye to Mrs. Bhatiya.

532
00:47:40.583 --> 00:47:42.375
She's fled from there.

533
00:47:42.458 --> 00:47:45.041
Her daughter-in-law beat her up.

534
00:47:45.875 --> 00:47:47.250
I know everything.

535
00:47:48.083 --> 00:47:49.791
So, shall we invite her for kitty?

536
00:47:50.208 --> 00:47:52.375
Forget it, dear. Why bother?

537
00:47:52.458 --> 00:47:55.541
I don't want to hear sob stories at kitty.

538
00:49:04.250 --> 00:49:07.625
Phoolchand! Hey, Phoolchand!

539
00:49:49.458 --> 00:49:50.458
Hey!

540
00:49:52.166 --> 00:49:54.708
You're stealing? You're stealing?
You're stealing?

541
00:49:54.791 --> 00:49:57.916
No! Hey! I'll get hurt! I'll get hurt!

542
00:50:00.083 --> 00:50:02.708
- I'll get hurt.
- Help! Help! Thief!

543
00:50:02.791 --> 00:50:05.291
Somebody help me! Is anybody there?

544
00:50:43.041 --> 00:50:45.291
Should I get tea or coffee?
Check the register.

545
00:50:45.375 --> 00:50:46.708
Take a look here. See this.

546
00:50:46.791 --> 00:50:49.583
- What happened?
- There was a theft here last night.

547
00:50:49.666 --> 00:50:51.208
- Where?
- The foreigner's house.

548
00:50:51.291 --> 00:50:52.291
- Really?
- Yeah.

549
00:50:52.375 --> 00:50:53.625
She's an Indian, right?

550
00:50:53.708 --> 00:50:57.875
Sir, this guy in the blue shirt
loiters around here every day.

551
00:50:57.958 --> 00:51:01.083
In mornings and evenings.
He just keeps staring at the balcony.

552
00:51:01.166 --> 00:51:03.625
That's the problem with singles.
I was robbed, too.

553
00:51:05.875 --> 00:51:08.708
Sir, this is Mrs. Prakash Kaur Handa.

554
00:51:08.791 --> 00:51:11.166
- There was a theft at her home.
- What was stolen?

555
00:51:11.250 --> 00:51:15.958
Sir, she's come from abroad,
so dollars, Indian currency etc.

556
00:51:16.666 --> 00:51:18.083
Some jewelry too.

557
00:51:18.166 --> 00:51:20.375
Earrings, bangles. How much in all?

558
00:51:20.458 --> 00:51:21.500
Around 200,000.

559
00:51:21.583 --> 00:51:22.958
Yeah, around 200,000.

560
00:51:23.041 --> 00:51:26.875
Did the guy
attack you with a knife or anything?

561
00:51:26.958 --> 00:51:28.500
No. Nothing like that happened.

562
00:51:28.583 --> 00:51:30.666
Sir, step into the light.

563
00:51:35.083 --> 00:51:37.375
Do... Do you know him?

564
00:51:38.208 --> 00:51:39.958
- No.
- What?

565
00:51:40.708 --> 00:51:43.708
What were you doing
under her building for the past ten days?

566
00:51:45.916 --> 00:51:47.208
I was surveying.

567
00:51:47.291 --> 00:51:49.416
- What were you doing?
- Survey.

568
00:51:49.875 --> 00:51:51.333
- What?
- Survey! Survey!

569
00:51:51.416 --> 00:51:52.833
What kind of survey?

570
00:51:53.666 --> 00:51:56.625
Survey of those people's houses
who live alone.

571
00:51:57.125 --> 00:52:00.333
You only advised me
to make friends and not stay alone.

572
00:52:00.416 --> 00:52:02.791
Come here. Sit down.

573
00:52:06.083 --> 00:52:08.916
How do you know that she lives alone?

574
00:52:09.375 --> 00:52:10.750
Told you, I did the survey.

575
00:52:11.125 --> 00:52:13.166
You mean you followed her?

576
00:52:13.250 --> 00:52:16.958
After exploring here and there,
I realized after seven days

577
00:52:17.041 --> 00:52:22.000
that the burglar might also
be doing the same surveying like me.

578
00:52:22.083 --> 00:52:25.333
- How are you so confident?
- There was a theft, right?

579
00:52:25.416 --> 00:52:27.000
Then, why didn't you tell?

580
00:52:27.416 --> 00:52:29.166
- I was about to.
- Then?

581
00:52:29.250 --> 00:52:32.708
First, I thought I'll befriend her.

582
00:52:33.500 --> 00:52:37.500
But the theft happened
before I could do that.

583
00:52:42.375 --> 00:52:44.916
Good, the prediction is good.

584
00:52:45.375 --> 00:52:46.958
Want to be an informant for us?

585
00:52:52.750 --> 00:52:55.125
- Can I leave?
- Yes, please.

586
00:52:55.208 --> 00:52:56.958
- Ms. Dhome...
- Yes, sir.

587
00:52:57.041 --> 00:52:59.125
Ma'am, do call us, if you face any issues.

588
00:52:59.208 --> 00:53:01.125
- Ms. Dhome, share my number.
- Yes, sir.

589
00:53:02.041 --> 00:53:03.166
<i>Namaste.</i>

590
00:53:03.250 --> 00:53:04.583
Sir...

591
00:53:09.833 --> 00:53:12.083
Who is the next target
for your friendship?

592
00:53:13.291 --> 00:53:14.291
Tell me, sir.

593
00:53:19.166 --> 00:53:21.666
JILA CIRCLE MAIN CHAUKI

594
00:53:23.916 --> 00:53:26.500
Please come, ma'am. Please sit inside.

595
00:53:44.625 --> 00:53:46.875
Hey! This psycho followed me here too?

596
00:53:47.500 --> 00:53:48.750
Is anybody there?

597
00:53:49.166 --> 00:53:53.125
- Inspector Mane!
- Hey, I... I have a similar case.

598
00:53:53.208 --> 00:53:55.625
- What case?
- Case of loneliness.

599
00:53:55.708 --> 00:53:57.583
- What?
- Lone...

600
00:54:01.500 --> 00:54:04.250
Let Inspector Mane come.
He will make you...

601
00:54:04.333 --> 00:54:05.375
Hey, ma'am.

602
00:54:05.458 --> 00:54:07.833
- Shut up, shut up!
- What are you doing, ma'am?

603
00:54:07.916 --> 00:54:10.916
- What a mess I am in! Fuck!
- Hey, ma'am.

604
00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:13.583
Let's go. Everything is ready.
We've found four suspects.

605
00:54:13.666 --> 00:54:15.416
I am not going to sit with that guy.

606
00:54:15.500 --> 00:54:18.708
Ma'am, he is Kamath.
There was a theft at his house too.

607
00:54:18.791 --> 00:54:20.250
He was even hit on the face.

608
00:54:20.333 --> 00:54:23.041
- Who else lives in his house?
- He lives by himself.

609
00:54:23.125 --> 00:54:24.250
He seems crazy.

610
00:54:24.791 --> 00:54:27.125
No, ma'am. He is not crazy.

611
00:54:27.208 --> 00:54:29.583
He is a very good man.
Go on, don't be scared.

612
00:54:30.250 --> 00:54:33.291
Do me a favor.
Give one to him, and wear one yourself.

613
00:54:33.375 --> 00:54:35.541
Please go. Don't worry. Please go.

614
00:54:39.333 --> 00:54:41.291
- Here.
- Thank you.

615
00:54:44.958 --> 00:54:46.000
Don't worry.

616
00:54:47.750 --> 00:54:48.916
Suspect number one.

617
00:54:51.041 --> 00:54:52.625
Suspect number two.

618
00:54:53.250 --> 00:54:54.833
Suspect number three.

619
00:54:55.791 --> 00:54:57.625
Suspect number four.

620
00:54:58.166 --> 00:54:59.541
Identification parade over.

621
00:55:37.416 --> 00:55:39.375
I thought you are a psycho.

622
00:55:40.500 --> 00:55:41.416
- Psycho?
- Yeah.

623
00:55:41.500 --> 00:55:47.166
Those who stalk people, scare them
with knives and daggers

624
00:55:47.250 --> 00:55:49.166
like those in English movies.

625
00:55:49.250 --> 00:55:51.083
Just a minute. Just a minute, ma'am.

626
00:55:51.166 --> 00:55:55.916
- When did I stalk you with knives?
- You did follow me, didn't you?

627
00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:57.500
I am sorry for that.

628
00:55:58.541 --> 00:56:01.375
No, I should be
the one apologizing to you.

629
00:56:01.458 --> 00:56:02.875
I misunderstood you.

630
00:56:02.958 --> 00:56:07.416
The fact is that in today's world
one cannot think straight.

631
00:56:07.500 --> 00:56:10.833
- See, I do surveys...
- Survey?

632
00:56:10.958 --> 00:56:13.041
- Yes.
- So, you used to be a surveyor?

633
00:56:13.125 --> 00:56:15.583
No, I worked with Zodox Company.

634
00:56:15.666 --> 00:56:20.083
In quality control.
I used to check the efficacy of drugs.

635
00:56:21.666 --> 00:56:27.166
You tasted
the drugs to check their efficacy?

636
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:36.541
Listen, please, don't get me wrong.

637
00:56:51.125 --> 00:56:52.125
Hi.

638
00:56:54.541 --> 00:56:56.708
Isn't Prakash a masculine name?

639
00:56:56.833 --> 00:57:00.541
No. It's Prakash Kaur.
It's quite common with Punjabis.

640
00:57:00.666 --> 00:57:03.458
Vikas Kaur, Sandeep Kaur, Kuldeep Kaur.

641
00:57:03.541 --> 00:57:05.750
That's how Madrasis are too, right?

642
00:57:05.833 --> 00:57:09.708
K.P.L.M. Prasad, T.V.K. Murdagaus.

643
00:57:09.791 --> 00:57:12.458
- And what about...
- I am not a Madrasi.

644
00:57:12.541 --> 00:57:14.166
You are not a Madrasi?

645
00:57:14.250 --> 00:57:15.583
- No.
- Then, what are you?

646
00:57:15.666 --> 00:57:17.458
Karnataka Karwar.

647
00:57:17.541 --> 00:57:19.708
You are a Madrasi from Karnataka.

648
00:57:19.791 --> 00:57:20.666
No.

649
00:57:20.750 --> 00:57:23.041
From the Karnataka-Maharashtra border.

650
00:57:23.125 --> 00:57:25.875
I speak both Kannadiga
and Marathi languages.

651
00:57:25.958 --> 00:57:28.500
- You are a Marathi?
- I'm not from Maharashtra.

652
00:57:28.583 --> 00:57:30.333
I am from Karwar.

653
00:57:30.416 --> 00:57:33.625
- Karwari Madrasi?
- Kannadiga.

654
00:57:35.041 --> 00:57:37.041
So Kannadiga Madrasi, right?

655
00:57:37.125 --> 00:57:39.375
Not everybody in the south is Madrasi.

656
00:57:39.458 --> 00:57:42.208
Ours is simple.
Anybody asks, "Who are you?"

657
00:57:42.291 --> 00:57:43.916
Punjabi from Punjab.

658
00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:49.625
Whether you're in London, USA or Canada,
you're a Punjabi. That's it, fucker!

659
00:57:51.708 --> 00:57:53.875
- Did you just swear?
- What?

660
00:57:54.416 --> 00:57:55.416
You swore?

661
00:58:32.833 --> 00:58:34.958
My dear brother. My dear brother.

662
00:58:35.041 --> 00:58:38.083
- Please give me some food.
- What brother? Get away from the car!

663
00:58:38.166 --> 00:58:41.166
Uncle, you wait here.
I have to do some work. Okay?

664
00:59:10.291 --> 00:59:11.458
Did you stitch it?

665
00:59:13.666 --> 00:59:14.666
For me?

666
00:59:18.916 --> 00:59:21.041
Shall I wear this and stand at the lights?

667
00:59:21.125 --> 00:59:24.375
No, this is for going out somewhere.

668
00:59:24.708 --> 00:59:25.750
I am outside.

669
00:59:26.375 --> 00:59:29.375
I mean to watch a movie and all.

670
00:59:29.875 --> 00:59:31.458
That would be inside, isn't it?

671
01:00:23.166 --> 01:00:24.458
You finally started?

672
01:00:24.541 --> 01:00:25.791
I am not looking for clients.

673
01:00:25.875 --> 01:00:29.125
- Then? Are you going to get married?
- Yeah.

674
01:01:32.166 --> 01:01:34.000
The hottie is a great dancer!

675
01:01:35.291 --> 01:01:37.375
What a dancer!

676
01:01:42.000 --> 01:01:43.458
- Do you know my real name?
- What?

677
01:01:46.083 --> 01:01:47.291
Rani.

678
01:01:48.791 --> 01:01:50.958
- Are you a Hindu?
- I don't know.

679
01:01:52.666 --> 01:01:54.291
I could be a Muslim as well.

680
01:01:56.250 --> 01:01:58.208
- What are you?
- Hindu.

681
01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:00.500
Madahosh Gupta.

682
01:02:01.291 --> 01:02:03.375
People call me "Nanhe, Nanhe" lovingly.

683
01:02:05.083 --> 01:02:08.083
- "Nanhe, Nanhe"?
- Hey, just Nanhe.

684
01:02:10.750 --> 01:02:12.416
Shut up, Chocobar!

685
01:02:13.291 --> 01:02:15.208
Why, is your mom giving birth?

686
01:02:29.791 --> 01:02:30.833
Hey!

687
01:02:31.666 --> 01:02:34.708
He is wearing all red.
He'll have a bull chasing him.

688
01:02:34.791 --> 01:02:38.583
It's a myth.
Bulls don't go after red clothes.

689
01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:41.250
Red!

690
01:02:51.208 --> 01:02:52.666
What's with the drama?

691
01:02:52.750 --> 01:02:57.416
- What were you doing?
- He can't hear, he has those things on.

692
01:02:59.750 --> 01:03:01.833
<i>This thing, that thing
This thing, that thing</i>

693
01:03:03.500 --> 01:03:05.541
<i>DiCosta, DiCosta, Fernandes</i>

694
01:03:07.875 --> 01:03:11.625
In this world, everybody is bound
to go crazy once in their lifetime.

695
01:03:12.166 --> 01:03:14.875
People act normal out of fear.

696
01:03:14.958 --> 01:03:16.375
I like craziness.

697
01:03:16.958 --> 01:03:18.625
Your energy is something else.

698
01:03:18.708 --> 01:03:24.375
You talk so much, add jokes in your talks
and then you laugh so much

699
01:03:24.458 --> 01:03:26.125
that it goes on and on!

700
01:03:26.875 --> 01:03:29.458
- So, what's wrong in that? Yes.
- It's very good.

701
01:03:29.541 --> 01:03:33.833
Look at me,
I don't even know to laugh at myself.

702
01:03:34.416 --> 01:03:37.083
I am talking to a woman
after 12 years.

703
01:03:37.458 --> 01:03:42.625
Whenever I talked to men,
they just swore, complained and taunted.

704
01:03:43.291 --> 01:03:45.041
They never talked about mankind,

705
01:03:45.125 --> 01:03:49.958
health, music, dance, gossip, happiness,

706
01:03:50.041 --> 01:03:52.041
dance and all that.

707
01:03:59.208 --> 01:04:02.208
Sorry, I've never talked so much.

708
01:04:07.666 --> 01:04:08.958
Sorry, I went blank.

709
01:04:10.416 --> 01:04:11.625
No worries.

710
01:04:12.666 --> 01:04:14.916
If you remember something, say it.

711
01:04:15.541 --> 01:04:17.041
If it doesn't, then don't say.

712
01:04:17.125 --> 01:04:20.166
But if you want to talk
about any topic, just say it.

713
01:04:20.250 --> 01:04:22.000
But life is not a topic.

714
01:04:22.666 --> 01:04:26.250
Nor is it a calculator,
that ten plus ten is equal to 20.

715
01:04:28.833 --> 01:04:32.208
You know, a raw mango, the sour one,
with salt.

716
01:04:33.125 --> 01:04:36.458
When you see that

717
01:04:36.541 --> 01:04:40.875
and your mouth drools,

718
01:04:41.708 --> 01:04:44.041
that's exactly what life is.

719
01:04:44.833 --> 01:04:48.583
When you stop drooling,
that fucks up your life.

720
01:04:49.375 --> 01:04:52.083
I learn a lot when I'm with you.

721
01:04:52.166 --> 01:04:56.500
Hey! Don't jinx it, I just love talking.

722
01:04:56.583 --> 01:04:58.833
But there should be someone to talk to.

723
01:04:58.916 --> 01:05:02.208
If I talk to myself, people will send me
to the nuthouse. Fuckers!

724
01:05:02.750 --> 01:05:04.166
I talk to myself.

725
01:05:12.083 --> 01:05:13.333
Now you won't.

726
01:05:39.500 --> 01:05:40.583
Ma'am.

727
01:05:43.875 --> 01:05:46.250
- Give it to me.
- No, it's mine.

728
01:06:03.083 --> 01:06:06.833
Four kids.
Doesn't the mom look a bit too young?

729
01:06:08.125 --> 01:06:09.791
I was also carrying a child.

730
01:06:12.375 --> 01:06:13.791
But I aborted it.

731
01:06:15.083 --> 01:06:17.333
Becoming a mother is bloody fucked.

732
01:06:18.208 --> 01:06:21.125
Our bodies go through so much.

733
01:06:21.666 --> 01:06:25.791
First, these are formed.
Then, these grow slowly.

734
01:06:26.541 --> 01:06:27.791
Blood from down there.

735
01:06:29.041 --> 01:06:33.833
Men keep ogling at us
from top to bottom all the time.

736
01:06:35.708 --> 01:06:37.166
The way they look at you,

737
01:06:37.250 --> 01:06:39.750
like the clothes will rip
and they will see it all.

738
01:06:42.916 --> 01:06:44.583
Where is your husband?

739
01:06:45.125 --> 01:06:46.541
What husband, man?

740
01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:49.791
I didn't marry that guy.

741
01:06:50.333 --> 01:06:51.708
His name was Rafeek.

742
01:06:51.791 --> 01:06:53.500
But he used to wear something...

743
01:06:54.125 --> 01:06:55.708
like a crucifix in his ear.

744
01:06:55.791 --> 01:06:57.541
We went on bike rides at night.

745
01:06:57.625 --> 01:06:59.291
He also used to get falooda for me.

746
01:07:00.166 --> 01:07:02.541
He had a passion for poetry.

747
01:07:02.625 --> 01:07:04.958
"In blood I pen this letter,
it's not plain you see.

748
01:07:05.041 --> 01:07:08.083
"Take me as your lover, baby,
a brother I don't want to be."

749
01:07:09.000 --> 01:07:10.250
Bloody, Rafeek.

750
01:07:11.500 --> 01:07:12.791
He moved to Dubai.

751
01:07:15.583 --> 01:07:18.958
There is nobody now. Nothing.

752
01:07:36.833 --> 01:07:38.416
They're pretty.

753
01:07:38.500 --> 01:07:42.250
What happened, Madrasi?
You seem to be lost in deep thoughts.

754
01:07:43.416 --> 01:07:47.291
- Nothing like that, just...
- If sea scares you, why didn't you say so?

755
01:07:47.375 --> 01:07:50.041
- We could've gone to the mall.
- That's not the issue.

756
01:07:52.166 --> 01:07:54.041
I am not scared of the sea.

757
01:07:55.750 --> 01:07:58.291
I feel sorry for the waves.

758
01:07:58.625 --> 01:08:02.416
Bashing against the rocks day after day,
crying out for help.

759
01:08:02.500 --> 01:08:04.291
But how does anyone help them?

760
01:08:04.875 --> 01:08:06.083
You cannot catch them.

761
01:08:06.958 --> 01:08:09.208
If you put them in a pail,
they turn to salty water.

762
01:08:09.916 --> 01:08:11.166
The waves dies.

763
01:08:12.375 --> 01:08:16.916
Mrs. Handa, I am sure that I am a wave.

764
01:08:17.750 --> 01:08:19.708
I am stuck in the curse of good health.

765
01:08:21.625 --> 01:08:23.333
- Madrasi?
- Yeah?

766
01:08:24.333 --> 01:08:26.750
There are two types of circles in life.

767
01:08:27.208 --> 01:08:29.666
One is the life we live.

768
01:08:30.208 --> 01:08:31.666
That is over.

769
01:08:31.750 --> 01:08:35.375
And the other, where life lives us.

770
01:08:36.750 --> 01:08:38.458
The one that's going on right now.

771
01:09:02.583 --> 01:09:04.416
Dubai is across the sea, right?

772
01:09:05.166 --> 01:09:06.333
Yeah, might be.

773
01:09:07.833 --> 01:09:10.500
So half the water is ours
and the other theirs, right?

774
01:09:10.583 --> 01:09:12.458
Yeah, something of that sort.

775
01:09:12.541 --> 01:09:13.708
Right.

776
01:09:13.791 --> 01:09:16.791
Then the fish
must be enjoying both the sides.

777
01:09:16.875 --> 01:09:18.041
Yeah.

778
01:09:19.333 --> 01:09:21.708
Bloody, us humans are stuck here.

779
01:09:21.791 --> 01:09:23.500
- If you are poor, then...
- Hey!

780
01:09:24.333 --> 01:09:26.458
You are always cribbing, man.

781
01:09:27.083 --> 01:09:28.125
Bloody, crybaby!

782
01:09:28.791 --> 01:09:30.041
No, Actually...

783
01:09:30.791 --> 01:09:34.458
The thing is that
when you are out in the open,

784
01:09:34.541 --> 01:09:35.666
the brain also frees up.

785
01:09:36.541 --> 01:09:39.541
I want a room with a skylight, you know.

786
01:09:40.791 --> 01:09:44.666
It's been years
since I saw the sky lying in bed.

787
01:09:44.750 --> 01:09:47.333
In the city, you cannot
even see the stars clearly.

788
01:09:48.291 --> 01:09:52.083
You know, in our village,
the sky is crystal clear.

789
01:09:52.666 --> 01:09:56.666
When we were small, we used to
start counting the stars from one end

790
01:09:56.750 --> 01:10:00.416
and went on to the other end.
Counting ended, but the stars didn't.

791
01:10:01.000 --> 01:10:02.333
What do you mean by "we"?

792
01:10:02.416 --> 01:10:05.166
Me and <i>Badkau,</i> my elder brother.

793
01:10:10.041 --> 01:10:11.416
Have you ever slept with...

794
01:10:14.541 --> 01:10:17.625
- Have you ever slept with a girl?
- To count stars?

795
01:10:21.541 --> 01:10:24.125
Stars! Bloody hell!

796
01:10:25.500 --> 01:10:28.500
I never was attracted to anyone.

797
01:10:30.625 --> 01:10:32.125
Are you attracted to me?

798
01:10:34.375 --> 01:10:38.541
Attraction happens on its own,
and not when one wants to.

799
01:10:38.625 --> 01:10:39.791
What about now?

800
01:10:41.000 --> 01:10:46.000
Now in this dress, you are looking good.
I want to look at you.

801
01:10:46.083 --> 01:10:47.583
What if I take off the dress?

802
01:10:49.625 --> 01:10:52.958
I've never talked
to any girl about all this.

803
01:10:53.041 --> 01:10:54.041
About what?

804
01:10:54.666 --> 01:10:56.250
About the birds and the bees.

805
01:11:07.291 --> 01:11:09.708
Nobody ever made me laugh so much, man.

806
01:11:14.208 --> 01:11:17.250
- Will you meet me every day?
- Yes.

807
01:12:34.250 --> 01:12:35.250
Does this open?

808
01:12:37.833 --> 01:12:40.291
I've never thought about it.
Maybe it does.

809
01:12:52.958 --> 01:12:54.250
Hey, Nanhe!

810
01:13:01.791 --> 01:13:03.833
Hey, whose is this?

811
01:13:05.333 --> 01:13:06.750
This is my mother's.

812
01:13:10.708 --> 01:13:11.833
Here.

813
01:13:16.375 --> 01:13:17.375
You keep it.

814
01:13:20.416 --> 01:13:21.500
Keep it.

815
01:13:22.458 --> 01:13:23.458
No.

816
01:13:23.541 --> 01:13:25.458
- Take it.
- No!

817
01:13:25.541 --> 01:13:28.166
Keep it, don't worry. Take it.

818
01:13:28.875 --> 01:13:29.875
You keep it.

819
01:13:33.791 --> 01:13:34.791
No.

820
01:13:34.875 --> 01:13:36.583
- Wear it.
- Here, take it.

821
01:13:36.666 --> 01:13:39.125
You can wear it later.

822
01:13:40.375 --> 01:13:41.833
I'm not going to take it back.

823
01:14:48.666 --> 01:14:50.000
<i>Namaste.</i>

824
01:14:50.083 --> 01:14:53.083
- Where's the rest, man?
- I'll pay you, sir.

825
01:14:54.375 --> 01:14:57.791
You are enjoying a lot
with this street girl.

826
01:14:58.583 --> 01:15:02.333
I'll bury you and Baburam alive, you wait.

827
01:15:02.416 --> 01:15:06.875
Return the 50,000 pronto,
or your shop will be shut down.

828
01:15:06.958 --> 01:15:11.208
Nanhe, you won't get a warning next time.
You'll be thrown out on the street.

829
01:15:27.708 --> 01:15:32.250
When the boy approaches the girl,
she will tuck her tummy in.

830
01:15:32.708 --> 01:15:37.125
Look. And as soon as he leaves,
she will release her tummy.

831
01:15:38.208 --> 01:15:43.125
See, it's nice
to observe things carefully at this age.

832
01:15:43.208 --> 01:15:46.375
It means that your brain is working right.

833
01:15:48.500 --> 01:15:52.791
This beauty spot of yours is a little big.

834
01:15:52.875 --> 01:15:55.541
It has three hairs, like a beard.

835
01:15:55.625 --> 01:15:57.125
I observed that.

836
01:15:59.958 --> 01:16:03.291
This beauty spot of mine
which is a little big,

837
01:16:03.833 --> 01:16:07.916
receives signals from Mars.

838
01:16:08.250 --> 01:16:11.208
- Handa home, Handa home.
- Are you kidding?

839
01:16:11.291 --> 01:16:14.750
You shouldn't observe
certain things about women,

840
01:16:14.833 --> 01:16:16.291
you shouldn't even see them.

841
01:16:16.375 --> 01:16:19.916
She is fat. She hasn't dyed her hair.
She has fake teeth.

842
01:16:20.000 --> 01:16:22.000
No! You shouldn't see.

843
01:16:22.083 --> 01:16:25.625
Even if there is something off
about a woman, consider her to be perfect.

844
01:16:26.083 --> 01:16:28.083
I shall. I was unaware of all this.

845
01:16:28.166 --> 01:16:30.291
So many men roam in the park

846
01:16:30.375 --> 01:16:33.375
with hair sticking out of their nose,
their ears.

847
01:16:33.458 --> 01:16:34.458
Doesn't it look gross?

848
01:16:34.541 --> 01:16:38.750
Nose hair is needed, dear.
They work as filters for pollution.

849
01:16:38.833 --> 01:16:40.375
Then make filter coffee!

850
01:16:41.208 --> 01:16:45.625
You'll make filter coffee
with nose hair. Bloody hell!

851
01:16:45.708 --> 01:16:50.125
I don't understand
why God has put hair everywhere.

852
01:16:50.708 --> 01:16:54.458
Now, women have hair
on legs, on arms.

853
01:16:54.541 --> 01:16:57.000
Sometimes they even have
a moustache and beard.

854
01:16:57.083 --> 01:16:58.125
Why, man?

855
01:17:00.541 --> 01:17:01.541
Come on.

856
01:17:02.250 --> 01:17:04.291
- Come on.
- Where are you taking me, Madrasi?

857
01:17:04.375 --> 01:17:06.458
You are my survey partner from today.

858
01:17:06.541 --> 01:17:11.166
I followed you for a whole week.
I know your whole schedule.

859
01:17:12.375 --> 01:17:14.458
The thief must have done the same, right?

860
01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:31.541
Red rabbit.

861
01:17:35.833 --> 01:17:37.750
Right side. First floor.

862
01:17:38.583 --> 01:17:39.750
You see?

863
01:17:40.583 --> 01:17:44.208
JEEVAN SUDHA

864
01:17:46.083 --> 01:17:47.291
He's looking this way!

865
01:17:56.833 --> 01:17:59.000
- Hey. Madrasi!
- Just a minute.

866
01:18:05.958 --> 01:18:07.166
Both the flats belong to him.

867
01:18:07.833 --> 01:18:09.333
Handamma! Handamma!

868
01:18:14.416 --> 01:18:17.458
I was a little rude yesterday,
I'm sorry for that.

869
01:18:17.541 --> 01:18:19.083
What a great survey partner!

870
01:18:19.166 --> 01:18:21.250
Actually, Randheer had also called.

871
01:18:21.333 --> 01:18:23.291
By the way, what work does Randheer do?

872
01:18:23.375 --> 01:18:26.958
He is an aeronautical engineer.
He's been in Canada for the past 10 years.

873
01:18:27.458 --> 01:18:30.208
He works at that company, Boeing Expo.

874
01:18:30.291 --> 01:18:32.125
- Is he at a high post?
- Yeah.

875
01:18:32.750 --> 01:18:36.000
He got married all of a sudden.
We couldn't even attend.

876
01:18:36.083 --> 01:18:37.708
My husband scolded him a lot.

877
01:18:38.833 --> 01:18:41.791
Then the fool surprised us that

878
01:18:41.875 --> 01:18:46.291
my granddaughter, Leela,
was born out of wedlock.

879
01:18:46.791 --> 01:18:52.458
Then he sent Leela's photo,
and we both just melted.

880
01:18:53.750 --> 01:18:55.708
She is so sweet.

881
01:18:56.791 --> 01:18:59.458
- Both her cheeks have dimples.
- Really?

882
01:18:59.541 --> 01:19:00.875
She calls me by my name.

883
01:19:01.625 --> 01:19:04.833
"Pakach, Pakach! Hey, Pakach!"

884
01:19:04.916 --> 01:19:08.708
She cannot pronounce "sh",
so she says "ch".

885
01:19:08.791 --> 01:19:10.416
She doesn't have any teeth yet.

886
01:19:12.000 --> 01:19:13.500
Oh, Leela.

887
01:19:14.625 --> 01:19:16.458
And Mr. Handa...

888
01:19:17.416 --> 01:19:18.625
It's been three years.

889
01:19:20.875 --> 01:19:22.833
They are both busy,

890
01:19:25.125 --> 01:19:27.166
so they couldn't even
make it to the memorial.

891
01:19:27.250 --> 01:19:28.250
I see.

892
01:19:41.750 --> 01:19:43.125
Hey, Bimla.

893
01:19:44.125 --> 01:19:45.750
Sonu, do not touch me.

894
01:19:45.833 --> 01:19:49.750
- I have to pay for the unit, Bimla.
- Why are you bothering me?

895
01:19:49.833 --> 01:19:53.791
- Bimla, I have to talk to you.
- I don't want to talk to you.

896
01:19:53.875 --> 01:19:56.208
Here, pack these three extra dresses.
Hurry up.

897
01:19:56.291 --> 01:19:58.625
<i>- Can you hear me, sister?</i>
- Yes, Nanhe. Tell me.

898
01:19:58.708 --> 01:20:03.208
I've got the sample of the cloth
that you had told me to get.

899
01:20:03.291 --> 01:20:05.875
It cost a lot, ma'am. It's very expensive.

900
01:20:07.000 --> 01:20:09.125
When are you coming back from Dubai?

901
01:20:09.208 --> 01:20:11.666
I am still here only.
I am leaving tonight.

902
01:20:11.750 --> 01:20:13.625
<i>That's going to mess up everything.</i>

903
01:20:13.708 --> 01:20:15.666
I need some advance.

904
01:20:15.750 --> 01:20:19.333
- So shall I come and get it from you?
- Nanhe, don't bore me.

905
01:20:19.416 --> 01:20:22.375
What kind of tailor are you?
When will you learn to roll?

906
01:20:22.458 --> 01:20:23.708
I mean...

907
01:20:23.791 --> 01:20:26.208
- Bimla, Bilkis! Do not mess with my mind.
<i>- Hello?</i>

908
01:20:26.291 --> 01:20:28.458
- Kill me. Don't you have any shame?
<i>- Hello?</i>

909
01:20:30.333 --> 01:20:31.333
<i>Hello?</i>

910
01:20:31.416 --> 01:20:35.000
Nanhe, I'm really overwhelmed with work!

911
01:20:35.791 --> 01:20:37.208
You come and see me next week.

912
01:20:39.541 --> 01:20:40.541
But...

913
01:20:42.625 --> 01:20:43.625
Damn it.

914
01:20:54.333 --> 01:20:56.291
- Glory to God.
- What's this, Nanhe?

915
01:20:56.375 --> 01:20:59.958
I was getting Kacchi Dabeli
for you from Umargam, so I got delayed.

916
01:21:00.041 --> 01:21:03.500
This time I'm short by 40,000 rupees.

917
01:21:03.583 --> 01:21:05.500
- No, you better talk to Mr. Nanu.
- Yes.

918
01:21:05.583 --> 01:21:08.083
- Order that saffron drink.
- Yes.

919
01:21:08.166 --> 01:21:10.083
- I am calling him.
- Yes, talk to him.

920
01:21:10.166 --> 01:21:13.083
- Lotya, pick it up.
- Glory to God, Mr. Nanu.

921
01:21:13.708 --> 01:21:15.625
I am good, how are you doing?

922
01:21:15.708 --> 01:21:18.375
Mr. Nanu, I'm 40,000 rupees
short this time.

923
01:21:18.458 --> 01:21:23.166
Yeah. No, no, I'll pay.
I'll give the full amount next week.

924
01:21:23.791 --> 01:21:26.416
If you won't support me, who else will?

925
01:21:26.500 --> 01:21:28.458
Brother Nanhe, you'll go a long way!

926
01:21:38.333 --> 01:21:40.541
- Get inside.
- What's the matter?

927
01:21:45.416 --> 01:21:46.541
Where is my stuff?

928
01:21:47.458 --> 01:21:49.625
Sir... I was short of funds.

929
01:21:50.666 --> 01:21:53.208
Asshole! Was it your father's stuff?

930
01:21:53.291 --> 01:21:54.791
Should I sell your machine?

931
01:21:54.875 --> 01:21:57.708
- Tell me!
- Not sold, I just pawned it.

932
01:21:57.791 --> 01:21:59.666
Hey! Didn't I tell you to leave me alone?

933
01:21:59.750 --> 01:22:00.875
You get moving.

934
01:22:02.875 --> 01:22:05.541
He sold off all the expensive stuff.

935
01:22:05.625 --> 01:22:07.375
Who's going to pay me for it? His father?

936
01:22:07.458 --> 01:22:12.125
Baburam, I want my previous due of 50,000,
and together with this, total 550,000.

937
01:22:12.208 --> 01:22:14.083
Pay right now or vacate the place!

938
01:22:14.208 --> 01:22:17.291
- If he absconds tomorrow, who'll pay me?
- I will, I will.

939
01:22:17.375 --> 01:22:20.416
I don't know. He pawned it
or shoved it up his ass, I want it back.

940
01:22:20.500 --> 01:22:22.750
I'll show you, you motherfucker.

941
01:22:23.500 --> 01:22:24.833
Bloody bastard.

942
01:22:36.375 --> 01:22:37.833
You stole stuff?

943
01:22:38.416 --> 01:22:40.291
I really needed the funds.

944
01:22:40.541 --> 01:22:42.083
Needed funds.

945
01:22:42.166 --> 01:22:44.833
Do people start stealing
when they are in need?

946
01:22:47.750 --> 01:22:49.833
- Forgive me, brother.
- Let go of my hand.

947
01:22:51.708 --> 01:22:55.500
- Let go! Leave me out of it.
- Brother, I beg of you, forgive me.

948
01:22:55.583 --> 01:22:56.583
Get lost!

949
01:23:06.625 --> 01:23:08.916
RING THE BELL!

950
01:23:12.000 --> 01:23:14.833
Sonu sir, sweets for you.

951
01:23:16.541 --> 01:23:19.541
I worked with you
in the <i>Chandrakala</i> TV show.

952
01:23:19.625 --> 01:23:22.500
We did the shooting
in Kaalia Maidan, Film City.

953
01:23:22.583 --> 01:23:23.583
Film City.

954
01:23:23.666 --> 01:23:26.291
You remember, you had gotten
a 1,000 underpants stitched.

955
01:23:26.375 --> 01:23:28.958
With the tiger print, and elastic?

956
01:23:29.291 --> 01:23:30.375
I stitched them.

957
01:23:31.458 --> 01:23:33.875
Our Bimla ma'am
was Bilkis ma'am back then.

958
01:23:35.500 --> 01:23:38.375
- I am Nanhe. Nanhe, the tailor.
- Shut up, asshole.

959
01:23:39.541 --> 01:23:41.500
Your Bimla ma'am has run away.

960
01:23:42.000 --> 01:23:43.916
- Run away?
- Get lost, fucker!

961
01:23:44.000 --> 01:23:47.125
- Hey, Sonu sir. How could this be?
- Hey!

962
01:23:47.208 --> 01:23:49.166
I have delivered all the dresses.

963
01:23:49.250 --> 01:23:52.041
Sonu sir! I'll not be able to survive.
Give me my money.

964
01:23:52.125 --> 01:23:53.416
- Go away!
- I am not leaving.

965
01:23:53.500 --> 01:23:56.208
- Give me my money. I am not leaving.
- I'll thrash you!

966
01:24:00.125 --> 01:24:01.541
I am getting it.

967
01:24:14.791 --> 01:24:16.541
She ruined my life,

968
01:24:16.625 --> 01:24:18.583
- and you want your money?
- You're hitting...

969
01:24:18.666 --> 01:24:20.291
My money... It's my money!

970
01:24:21.166 --> 01:24:23.208
Did you ask me before taking the money?

971
01:24:38.916 --> 01:24:41.666
Is this for me? Sweater?

972
01:24:43.291 --> 01:24:44.291
Scarf?

973
01:24:44.375 --> 01:24:45.375
What is it then?

974
01:24:46.416 --> 01:24:48.125
This is a <i>toran</i> for the waves.

975
01:24:48.208 --> 01:24:49.541
I've brought it home.

976
01:24:49.916 --> 01:24:53.333
Stop calling yourself a wave
and hang this on the door.

977
01:25:09.333 --> 01:25:10.750
This is the club.

978
01:25:11.625 --> 01:25:13.458
Look, Sukhani is sitting there.

979
01:25:13.541 --> 01:25:15.041
He too lives alone?

980
01:25:15.166 --> 01:25:16.875
The wealthy loner.

981
01:25:22.083 --> 01:25:24.791
Such behavior is not appropriate
at the time of the survey.

982
01:25:26.875 --> 01:25:29.125
This is Sundar Sukhani's house.

983
01:25:29.208 --> 01:25:34.916
He is drinking at the bar and
all the lights are on, total waste.

984
01:25:38.291 --> 01:25:40.208
Hey! I saw someone there.

985
01:25:40.291 --> 01:25:43.041
- Look at the window.
- I just told you there's nobody at home.

986
01:25:43.125 --> 01:25:45.666
I just saw someone.

987
01:25:45.750 --> 01:25:47.583
He has no relatives, he stays alone.

988
01:25:47.666 --> 01:25:50.875
No, no. Call him. Let's do that.

989
01:25:50.958 --> 01:25:53.333
No, no. Call 100. Do it.

990
01:25:53.416 --> 01:25:55.625
What will I say after dialing the number?

991
01:25:55.708 --> 01:25:58.958
That we were surveying down here
and saw a thief up there?

992
01:25:59.041 --> 01:26:00.125
What do we do?

993
01:26:03.541 --> 01:26:05.916
- What are you doing? Don't go inside.
- One minute.

994
01:26:11.291 --> 01:26:12.916
- Who are you? Thief!
- I saw him!

995
01:26:13.000 --> 01:26:14.250
Where are you going?

996
01:26:14.333 --> 01:26:15.333
Thief! Thief!

997
01:26:18.666 --> 01:26:20.958
Hey, yellow t-shirt! Stop! Stop!

998
01:26:22.833 --> 01:26:25.375
What happened? Killed him! You killed him?

999
01:26:25.458 --> 01:26:27.375
- He ran away.
- Ran away!

1000
01:26:27.458 --> 01:26:31.333
Come on! Let us run too.
Come on! Let's leave this place.

1001
01:26:38.416 --> 01:26:39.875
Good night, dear.

1002
01:26:39.958 --> 01:26:41.541
- Bye.
- Good night, dear.

1003
01:26:41.625 --> 01:26:43.916
It's getting late.
I have to wake up early.

1004
01:26:46.083 --> 01:26:47.208
She's gone upstairs.

1005
01:26:51.125 --> 01:26:52.250
- She's gone.
- She's alone.

1006
01:26:52.333 --> 01:26:53.750
She's coming back.

1007
01:27:03.666 --> 01:27:04.708
She's gone.

1008
01:27:25.166 --> 01:27:27.666
- Let's leave.
- Wait for a couple of minutes.

1009
01:27:28.208 --> 01:27:30.541
How unscrupulous these thieves can be.

1010
01:27:30.625 --> 01:27:32.291
What do they even think?

1011
01:27:32.375 --> 01:27:33.916
Why are you thinking like a thief?

1012
01:27:34.000 --> 01:27:37.166
No harm in thinking, right?
We're not thieves.

1013
01:27:37.541 --> 01:27:39.916
Which is this painting?

1014
01:27:40.000 --> 01:27:42.708
- Mrs. Handa!
- Thirty-three, 34, 35...

1015
01:27:42.791 --> 01:27:43.833
Prakash!

1016
01:27:56.416 --> 01:27:57.625
Have you gone mad?

1017
01:27:58.291 --> 01:28:00.250
He won't be back till 11:00 pm.

1018
01:28:00.333 --> 01:28:03.083
Do you want to drink his beer till 10:45?

1019
01:28:03.166 --> 01:28:05.416
Yes, you were the one who said

1020
01:28:05.500 --> 01:28:10.375
that life is living us,
and this time won't come back.

1021
01:28:10.458 --> 01:28:11.750
It won't.

1022
01:28:22.708 --> 01:28:26.333
Hey! It's 10:45, bloody fucker!
Come on, get up!

1023
01:28:29.041 --> 01:28:30.208
Hurry up.

1024
01:28:31.250 --> 01:28:32.541
I'll turn off the light.

1025
01:28:53.250 --> 01:28:54.791
Good morning, Mr. Bhonsle.

1026
01:28:55.583 --> 01:28:57.791
Has anybody reported a theft?

1027
01:28:58.166 --> 01:28:59.041
What theft?

1028
01:28:59.125 --> 01:29:00.291
Like any...

1029
01:29:00.375 --> 01:29:02.166
Just that it's been so many days.

1030
01:29:02.333 --> 01:29:04.500
- No suspect was...
- was caught.

1031
01:29:04.583 --> 01:29:06.000
- Was caught.
- That's why.

1032
01:29:06.083 --> 01:29:08.625
Had we found something,
we would have called.

1033
01:29:10.416 --> 01:29:12.833
But this is good, you know,
what you both are doing.

1034
01:29:12.916 --> 01:29:15.041
Stick together. Okay?

1035
01:29:15.375 --> 01:29:17.375
And you should be alert at all times.

1036
01:29:19.208 --> 01:29:20.916
Yeah, Jitender! What's up?

1037
01:29:38.208 --> 01:29:39.416
Who is this guy?

1038
01:29:39.791 --> 01:29:42.291
Tabrez Panjwani, stays in lane four.

1039
01:29:42.375 --> 01:29:44.166
What was he saying in Sindhi?

1040
01:29:44.250 --> 01:29:47.791
He was saying that
he's leaving by flight tonight.

1041
01:29:47.875 --> 01:29:50.750
Some cheap Bharat Air
international flight.

1042
01:29:50.833 --> 01:29:52.250
The key is "under welcome".

1043
01:29:52.333 --> 01:29:53.625
What does "under welcome" mean?

1044
01:29:53.708 --> 01:29:56.750
Now, you don't start getting any ideas.

1045
01:29:56.833 --> 01:29:58.666
- Got it?
- Of course.

1046
01:29:58.750 --> 01:29:59.875
Totally over.

1047
01:29:59.958 --> 01:30:02.416
We had our fun once, had beer, that's it.

1048
01:30:02.750 --> 01:30:04.708
Right! We are not professional thieves.

1049
01:30:34.708 --> 01:30:36.500
- It's plastic.
- Madrasi!

1050
01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:51.833
- This is the last one, okay?
- The last one. Come on.

1051
01:31:08.666 --> 01:31:11.291
These girls...

1052
01:31:46.875 --> 01:31:47.875
Thief.

1053
01:31:48.875 --> 01:31:50.833
You are here to rob me?

1054
01:31:50.916 --> 01:31:53.250
But you live in Matru Maya.

1055
01:31:54.500 --> 01:31:56.166
Son of a bitch.

1056
01:31:56.250 --> 01:31:58.500
- Sir, no cussing.
- Cussing?

1057
01:31:59.500 --> 01:32:01.291
I'll show you cussing, wait.

1058
01:32:02.583 --> 01:32:04.375
I am talking to you calmly.

1059
01:32:04.458 --> 01:32:06.916
A thief expects me to talk calmly?

1060
01:32:07.000 --> 01:32:08.833
You've snuck in here too.

1061
01:32:08.916 --> 01:32:11.125
I know the person who lives here.

1062
01:32:11.208 --> 01:32:13.750
He is a Bengali guy,
he comes to walk in the park.

1063
01:32:14.416 --> 01:32:17.083
You did the robbery
in Dhavalgiri too, right?

1064
01:32:17.166 --> 01:32:19.375
Forget about what I did.

1065
01:32:19.708 --> 01:32:22.125
If you call the cops,
we both will be in trouble.

1066
01:32:22.583 --> 01:32:24.833
- Shall I call them?
- Go ahead.

1067
01:32:24.916 --> 01:32:27.625
- Shall I call them? Shall I?
- Go ahead. Yes. Yes.

1068
01:32:27.708 --> 01:32:28.791
I'm saying call them.

1069
01:32:29.208 --> 01:32:32.000
- Why did you hit him?
- I don't know!

1070
01:32:32.083 --> 01:32:34.083
Come on, now! "I don't know."

1071
01:32:34.166 --> 01:32:36.125
I don't know. Leave now.

1072
01:32:42.500 --> 01:32:44.125
- What happened?
- Watch your step.

1073
01:32:46.291 --> 01:32:48.125
What have you done?

1074
01:32:54.000 --> 01:32:55.708
Watch the steps. Careful.

1075
01:33:14.333 --> 01:33:16.208
What happened? Mrs. Handa!

1076
01:33:16.291 --> 01:33:18.375
Mrs. Handa, what happened?

1077
01:33:18.458 --> 01:33:20.666
What happened, dear? What is it?

1078
01:33:21.666 --> 01:33:23.458
I... I will get a cab.

1079
01:35:16.208 --> 01:35:17.583
What do you do for work?

1080
01:35:17.666 --> 01:35:18.750
I am a tailor.

1081
01:35:18.833 --> 01:35:19.958
How did this happen?

1082
01:35:20.333 --> 01:35:22.166
A pot fell on my head.

1083
01:35:22.583 --> 01:35:24.333
You should be more careful.

1084
01:35:26.625 --> 01:35:28.083
You've got four stitches.

1085
01:35:28.166 --> 01:35:30.791
No rice, potato, lemon for ten days.

1086
01:35:30.875 --> 01:35:33.125
Got it? There's a wound in your feet too.

1087
01:35:35.750 --> 01:35:38.625
You're taking the medicines
I prescribed last week, right?

1088
01:37:15.333 --> 01:37:18.208
Hey! Who are you?

1089
01:37:18.291 --> 01:37:21.250
- A lady was brought here...
- You cannot come here.

1090
01:37:21.333 --> 01:37:25.541
- Just once...
- No. Not at all. Leave. Go out. No.

1091
01:37:25.625 --> 01:37:27.458
- Just once...
- No, please go out.

1092
01:37:27.541 --> 01:37:29.500
Don't you understand?
I'll repeat 100 times?

1093
01:37:29.583 --> 01:37:31.250
- Out! Security!
- Just...

1094
01:37:31.333 --> 01:37:33.083
What are you doing outside? Come here.

1095
01:37:33.166 --> 01:37:35.458
He's trying to come inside the ICU.

1096
01:37:39.333 --> 01:37:40.250
Hey, stop!

1097
01:37:40.333 --> 01:37:42.416
<i>Bed number 127,</i> they've called you.

1098
01:38:06.208 --> 01:38:08.500
Seeing your nose...

1099
01:38:09.958 --> 01:38:12.625
up close...

1100
01:38:15.375 --> 01:38:19.208
reminded me of filter coffee.

1101
01:38:21.291 --> 01:38:24.333
Don't laugh so much.
After a few days you can.

1102
01:38:25.541 --> 01:38:27.500
Don't stop me, Madrasi.

1103
01:38:29.291 --> 01:38:33.333
I am laughing heartily
after three years.

1104
01:38:36.458 --> 01:38:39.375
My life was over.

1105
01:38:43.708 --> 01:38:45.791
My heart was beating,

1106
01:38:48.083 --> 01:38:49.666
so I was still alive.

1107
01:38:51.916 --> 01:38:56.958
Today, after so many years,
I want to live life again.

1108
01:39:00.625 --> 01:39:03.291
I was suffocating in Canada.

1109
01:39:05.000 --> 01:39:09.041
Oh, God. I was suffocating in Canada.

1110
01:39:16.791 --> 01:39:18.125
Forget about everything.

1111
01:39:19.458 --> 01:39:20.750
Now, we will live.

1112
01:39:21.291 --> 01:39:22.541
We will live...

1113
01:39:23.750 --> 01:39:25.250
just the way we want to.

1114
01:39:29.375 --> 01:39:30.375
Okay?

1115
01:39:35.250 --> 01:39:39.791
That thief...
That thief didn't die, right?

1116
01:39:41.291 --> 01:39:44.583
That thief...

1117
01:40:09.875 --> 01:40:11.000
<i>Babu...</i>

1118
01:40:38.583 --> 01:40:40.458
She makes very good Pav Bhaji.

1119
01:40:41.416 --> 01:40:43.666
No. I got the pav from the bakery.

1120
01:40:45.625 --> 01:40:47.500
It's upstairs, go.

1121
01:40:52.208 --> 01:40:53.500
<i>Will you marry her?</i>

1122
01:40:55.375 --> 01:40:56.541
What is her name?

1123
01:40:57.583 --> 01:40:58.666
Rani.

1124
01:40:58.750 --> 01:41:00.375
Rani!

1125
01:41:01.291 --> 01:41:03.791
Nanhe's Rani, is it?

1126
01:41:04.916 --> 01:41:07.333
You are brimming with happiness.

1127
01:41:07.916 --> 01:41:09.458
Now, do one thing.

1128
01:41:09.541 --> 01:41:12.958
Make her stop
the traffic lights business.

1129
01:41:13.041 --> 01:41:16.458
No, brother. She has quit all that.
She has changed.

1130
01:41:17.083 --> 01:41:20.833
Now, start selling eggs, chips,
pickles from house to house.

1131
01:41:21.625 --> 01:41:22.625
Take up that work.

1132
01:41:24.083 --> 01:41:25.208
Got it?

1133
01:41:25.750 --> 01:41:28.333
Why are you crying, dear?

1134
01:41:29.166 --> 01:41:30.916
You get me worried, man.

1135
01:41:31.708 --> 01:41:33.333
Shall I warm up the pav in oil?

1136
01:41:36.791 --> 01:41:39.291
- These are the bills. Please pay them.
- Yes.

1137
01:41:39.375 --> 01:41:41.875
- Meanwhile, I will prepare the discharge.
- Thank you.

1138
01:41:44.291 --> 01:41:45.708
How much is it?

1139
01:41:47.416 --> 01:41:49.708
Don't worry, we will talk about it later.

1140
01:41:52.083 --> 01:41:54.041
- Should we call Randheer?
- No.

1141
01:41:55.958 --> 01:41:57.833
Do you have insurance?

1142
01:42:00.041 --> 01:42:01.041
No.

1143
01:42:02.291 --> 01:42:03.291
Okay.

1144
01:42:14.166 --> 01:42:16.291
Two lakh fifty-five thousand.

1145
01:42:16.375 --> 01:42:17.666
Did you count it?

1146
01:42:17.750 --> 01:42:18.791
Yes.

1147
01:42:19.333 --> 01:42:22.125
Two lakh fifty-six thousand.

1148
01:43:05.458 --> 01:43:07.000
What are you doing here?

1149
01:43:08.666 --> 01:43:10.083
You're working as a hooker?

1150
01:43:13.291 --> 01:43:15.000
Have you lost your mind?

1151
01:43:17.083 --> 01:43:18.375
Why did you follow me?

1152
01:43:25.125 --> 01:43:27.125
Why do you have to do all this?

1153
01:43:28.125 --> 01:43:31.750
Who are you, man?
Who are you? Look at me.

1154
01:43:32.416 --> 01:43:34.333
Are you my father? My husband?

1155
01:43:35.125 --> 01:43:37.583
You had fun for a few days,
that makes me your property?

1156
01:43:38.166 --> 01:43:42.125
I told you that I'm there for you,
what's the need to do this?

1157
01:43:42.208 --> 01:43:44.833
It's my wish!

1158
01:43:47.875 --> 01:43:49.250
I like to sleep around, okay?

1159
01:43:50.708 --> 01:43:54.750
What will you do? Become my pimp?
Will you become my pimp?

1160
01:44:04.541 --> 01:44:07.000
What did you
accomplish with your business?

1161
01:44:07.416 --> 01:44:09.041
You are drowning in debt.

1162
01:45:36.958 --> 01:45:38.333
I need to use the washroom.

1163
01:46:21.541 --> 01:46:23.875
A train goes from platform number five.

1164
01:46:23.958 --> 01:46:27.250
You can see
a small family in every window.

1165
01:46:27.791 --> 01:46:29.250
You are from Ghazipur, right?

1166
01:46:29.583 --> 01:46:31.875
Ghazipur or Mumbai, it hardly matters now.

1167
01:46:34.291 --> 01:46:35.958
Every place is a swamp.

1168
01:46:38.083 --> 01:46:39.208
Do you have a family?

1169
01:46:40.166 --> 01:46:41.625
I have an elder brother.

1170
01:46:43.083 --> 01:46:44.333
Do you talk to him?

1171
01:46:46.458 --> 01:46:47.541
We don't get along.

1172
01:46:49.166 --> 01:46:50.916
I used to get along with my mother.

1173
01:46:51.500 --> 01:46:53.625
She cried a lot when I ran away from home.

1174
01:46:54.500 --> 01:46:56.208
I miss her a lot.

1175
01:46:56.291 --> 01:46:59.750
But if I go there now,
what if she is no more?

1176
01:47:00.875 --> 01:47:02.250
It will be really painful.

1177
01:47:03.666 --> 01:47:04.833
Why did you leave home?

1178
01:47:05.625 --> 01:47:07.541
Brother's door was smashed.

1179
01:47:07.958 --> 01:47:09.166
I smashed it.

1180
01:47:10.541 --> 01:47:13.041
Bloody sister-in-law complained.

1181
01:47:13.666 --> 01:47:16.958
So, brother beat Mom up
with a burning stick.

1182
01:47:20.250 --> 01:47:23.375
There's an animal
inside every human being.

1183
01:47:24.875 --> 01:47:25.958
It lies dormant.

1184
01:47:27.500 --> 01:47:31.916
But when it wakes up,
that's when a person starts sinning.

1185
01:47:32.708 --> 01:47:36.583
That is why, this city is making me
commit one sin after another.

1186
01:47:39.000 --> 01:47:40.208
What sin, man?

1187
01:47:41.583 --> 01:47:46.625
I broke into a house,
hit the guy, and broke his nose.

1188
01:47:46.875 --> 01:47:48.750
And stole jewelry, and fled.

1189
01:47:49.666 --> 01:47:50.958
Broke into another house.

1190
01:47:52.041 --> 01:47:54.458
She was my mother's age.

1191
01:47:55.541 --> 01:47:59.958
I pushed her,
wrapped her in a mattress and hit her.

1192
01:48:02.041 --> 01:48:04.583
She is in the hospital now.

1193
01:48:04.666 --> 01:48:05.916
She must have died.

1194
01:48:07.041 --> 01:48:08.291
I don't know.

1195
01:48:09.375 --> 01:48:11.500
Then, another house.

1196
01:48:12.166 --> 01:48:14.833
Then another, and another.

1197
01:48:17.625 --> 01:48:19.541
But now I am tired, Baburam.

1198
01:48:22.500 --> 01:48:24.000
I don't want anything now.

1199
01:48:26.875 --> 01:48:28.291
I want to go to my village.

1200
01:48:30.041 --> 01:48:32.666
What do I do? Shall I end my life?

1201
01:48:34.208 --> 01:48:36.625
I should end my life on these tracks.

1202
01:48:54.708 --> 01:48:56.833
What the hell is this city, man?

1203
01:49:01.125 --> 01:49:02.625
What is this life?

1204
01:49:41.291 --> 01:49:42.958
Hello, who is this?

1205
01:49:44.375 --> 01:49:45.625
Kamath who?

1206
01:49:45.708 --> 01:49:47.583
<i>Randheer... Is that Randheer?</i>

1207
01:49:47.666 --> 01:49:49.208
Sorry, I didn't recognize you.

1208
01:49:49.291 --> 01:49:51.958
I am your mom's friend from the park.

1209
01:49:52.041 --> 01:49:54.750
<i>- I didn't know that you were back.</i>
- I just came today.

1210
01:49:54.833 --> 01:49:57.041
<i>How's your little daughter, Leela?</i>

1211
01:49:57.125 --> 01:50:01.750
She calls your mother "Pakach-Pakach".
Very sweet.

1212
01:50:02.208 --> 01:50:07.000
- Is there anything urgent?
- I called your mom for dinner today.

1213
01:50:07.083 --> 01:50:09.708
<i>I am making Panipuri for her</i>

1214
01:50:09.791 --> 01:50:12.250
<i>and she is bringing Kadhi-Pakodi.</i>

1215
01:50:12.333 --> 01:50:15.250
- It would be nice, if you came along.
- She's gone to bed.

1216
01:50:15.666 --> 01:50:17.333
You can call tomorrow, please.

1217
01:50:17.416 --> 01:50:18.583
<i>Randheer?</i>

1218
01:50:24.291 --> 01:50:25.333
What are you doing?

1219
01:50:26.666 --> 01:50:28.083
I know what I am doing, Mom.

1220
01:50:28.166 --> 01:50:30.750
You had a heart attack.
There reports show alcohol.

1221
01:50:30.833 --> 01:50:34.208
- Is this your age to do all this?
- Is this how you talk to your mom?

1222
01:50:34.291 --> 01:50:35.375
What do you want?

1223
01:50:35.458 --> 01:50:38.791
Do you want me to be your wife's maid?
Is that what you want?

1224
01:50:38.875 --> 01:50:40.208
Then go to hell!

1225
01:51:11.000 --> 01:51:13.083
- It's good.
- Shall I serve some more?

1226
01:51:17.083 --> 01:51:18.083
Look, brother.

1227
01:51:19.916 --> 01:51:23.166
If you maintain kinship in business,
then you will be finished.

1228
01:51:23.250 --> 01:51:24.708
- Understood?
- Yes.

1229
01:51:25.375 --> 01:51:28.875
That's why I say,
run business according to business.

1230
01:51:28.958 --> 01:51:30.041
Enough. Enough.

1231
01:51:30.500 --> 01:51:31.625
Give some more.

1232
01:51:31.875 --> 01:51:32.916
Enough.

1233
01:51:33.000 --> 01:51:35.250
Look, friendship is one thing.

1234
01:51:36.041 --> 01:51:37.833
- Are you done?
- Yes.

1235
01:51:37.916 --> 01:51:39.875
I don't eat more than this at night.

1236
01:51:43.458 --> 01:51:44.791
Liyakat.

1237
01:51:51.375 --> 01:51:52.750
Why are you here?

1238
01:51:53.291 --> 01:51:56.250
Had I not come here,
how would I have known your status?

1239
01:52:00.750 --> 01:52:02.875
Are you marrying that tailor?

1240
01:52:04.708 --> 01:52:09.041
No, if I quit this work,
who will take care of people like you?

1241
01:52:11.416 --> 01:52:13.333
- Hey, whore!
- Say it loudly.

1242
01:52:13.416 --> 01:52:15.208
Shall I say it? "Whore!"

1243
01:52:17.375 --> 01:52:20.041
Look. Don't make a scene here.

1244
01:52:22.666 --> 01:52:23.750
Right.

1245
01:52:23.875 --> 01:52:27.708
My body is business for me, right?

1246
01:52:28.791 --> 01:52:33.500
Similarly, the day
you buy your own shop, you pimp,

1247
01:52:34.416 --> 01:52:36.166
only then will I respect you.

1248
01:52:51.000 --> 01:52:52.000
Sir.

1249
01:52:52.750 --> 01:52:54.041
Ma'am is not at home.

1250
01:52:55.166 --> 01:52:57.458
Okay, I will wait.

1251
01:52:57.541 --> 01:53:00.875
No. Look, sir,
if you stay here, I'll call the cops.

1252
01:53:01.791 --> 01:53:03.791
Give this to her.

1253
01:53:03.875 --> 01:53:05.833
I've been told not to take anything.

1254
01:53:07.750 --> 01:53:09.458
Please leave.

1255
01:53:30.333 --> 01:53:31.333
What's it?

1256
01:53:32.916 --> 01:53:33.916
What's it to you?

1257
01:53:34.000 --> 01:53:35.083
What are you doing?

1258
01:53:35.208 --> 01:53:37.250
- Hey, move. I'm leaving.
- Hey!

1259
01:53:37.333 --> 01:53:40.833
- Hey, I am going down. Leave me!
- What the hell are you doing here?

1260
01:53:40.916 --> 01:53:44.333
Hey! Stop! Phoolan!
The thief is running away! Catch him!

1261
01:53:44.750 --> 01:53:46.583
Asshole! Hey! Motherfucker!

1262
01:54:02.708 --> 01:54:04.250
- Good evening.
- Good evening, sir.

1263
01:54:04.333 --> 01:54:05.500
How are you, guys?

1264
01:54:05.583 --> 01:54:07.666
Police and extortion is bothering us, sir.

1265
01:54:07.750 --> 01:54:09.958
It's crowded, but nobody wants
to know their future.

1266
01:54:10.041 --> 01:54:11.708
They take selfies and get moving.

1267
01:54:11.791 --> 01:54:15.250
- Sir, would you please hear your future?
- Okay.

1268
01:54:16.833 --> 01:54:20.125
Astrological sign Taurus. 75 years old.

1269
01:54:22.833 --> 01:54:26.000
Astrological sign, Taurus.
Your life will be happy again.

1270
01:54:26.083 --> 01:54:28.250
Focus more on your health.

1271
01:54:32.750 --> 01:54:35.708
- Hello?
- Hello, Madrasi. I'm at the airport.

1272
01:54:36.541 --> 01:54:38.458
I am leaving for Canada. Bye.

1273
01:54:47.458 --> 01:54:48.750
The flight is on time.

1274
01:55:03.250 --> 01:55:06.875
<i>The number you have dialed
is currently busy.</i>

1275
01:55:06.958 --> 01:55:09.291
Drive a little faster, please.

1276
01:56:45.291 --> 01:56:47.291
One, two, three, four...
How long has it been?

1277
01:56:47.375 --> 01:56:48.250
Eight hours.

1278
01:56:48.333 --> 01:56:50.916
Shouldn't we get overtime for working
more than eight hours?

1279
01:56:51.000 --> 01:56:53.125
Why are we working for free here?

1280
01:56:53.208 --> 01:56:57.458
I work, you work,
this sir works, everybody works.

1281
01:56:57.541 --> 01:56:59.041
Then why don't they pay us?

1282
01:56:59.666 --> 01:57:01.500
What do they get by cutting our pay?

1283
01:57:03.666 --> 01:57:04.666
Sir.

1284
01:57:05.041 --> 01:57:06.708
- Thank you.
- It's homemade.

1285
01:57:06.791 --> 01:57:08.791
- No, thank you.
- My wife made it.

1286
01:57:13.083 --> 01:57:14.541
Did you miss the flight, sir?

1287
01:57:15.208 --> 01:57:16.875
I came here to see off someone.

1288
01:57:19.166 --> 01:57:22.958
But I was late.
The flight departed to Canada.

1289
01:57:23.916 --> 01:57:25.875
I don't know if we'll meet again or not.

1290
01:57:28.791 --> 01:57:34.458
Everything in life
either happens before time or after time.

1291
01:57:37.416 --> 01:57:39.291
Why doesn't anything happen on time?

1292
01:57:44.375 --> 01:57:45.750
I have no disease at all.

1293
01:57:51.125 --> 01:57:55.541
I tried a lot to live by the alarm.

1294
01:57:56.666 --> 01:57:58.166
To keep my distance from all.

1295
01:57:59.333 --> 01:58:02.041
I lived every day,
lived for a lot of days.

1296
01:58:05.291 --> 01:58:07.125
I don't need attachment now.

1297
01:58:09.541 --> 01:58:11.541
Do you know what is attachment, dear?

1298
01:58:12.125 --> 01:58:13.125
No?

1299
01:58:15.625 --> 01:58:18.500
Attachment is the most dangerous thing,

1300
01:58:19.166 --> 01:58:22.708
once it happens, then your
arrogance is destroyed

1301
01:58:23.291 --> 01:58:26.000
I was arrogant, why should I lie?

1302
01:58:28.083 --> 01:58:31.125
I was never so talkative.
I used to be reserved.

1303
01:58:32.625 --> 01:58:34.000
People took me to be crazy.

1304
01:58:35.583 --> 01:58:38.666
Now I've become talkative,
and you must think I am crazy.

1305
01:58:38.750 --> 01:58:41.166
- No, no.
- I don't care.

1306
01:58:43.583 --> 01:58:44.916
I tried to shield myself.

1307
01:58:46.541 --> 01:58:48.125
But somehow,

1308
01:58:48.833 --> 01:58:53.125
I still got trapped
in the video game of this city.

1309
01:58:53.833 --> 01:58:57.750
The player will fire a bullet,
you have to dodge it.

1310
01:58:58.166 --> 01:59:02.250
Me, him, you, the pilot,
all are in this game.

1311
01:59:03.000 --> 01:59:04.416
How long will we dodge?

1312
01:59:05.000 --> 01:59:08.166
Finally, one day you get hit.

1313
01:59:15.291 --> 01:59:16.541
The video game is over.

1314
01:59:17.375 --> 01:59:19.416
I'm still alive,
even after my game was over.

1315
01:59:19.833 --> 01:59:22.708
I got cheated. Fuck!

1316
01:59:23.208 --> 01:59:25.750
Fuck. Fuck!

1317
01:59:28.791 --> 01:59:31.500
Sorry, she used to say that. Sorry.

1318
01:59:34.375 --> 01:59:35.375
By the way...

1319
02:00:48.916 --> 02:00:52.375
When you go out, face up, mouth shut,
you get it? No drama!

1320
02:00:54.750 --> 02:00:56.750
If you recognize, then nod to say "yes".

1321
02:00:57.333 --> 02:00:59.000
Otherwise, "no".

1322
02:01:01.666 --> 02:01:03.458
Suspect number one.

1323
02:01:04.541 --> 02:01:06.291
Suspect number two.

1324
02:01:09.791 --> 02:01:11.333
Suspect number three.

1325
02:01:26.541 --> 02:01:28.083
All done.

1326
02:01:40.833 --> 02:01:43.291
What are you staring at, Madrasi?

1327
02:01:58.916 --> 02:02:00.166
But you...

1328
02:02:01.250 --> 02:02:03.583
I got a signal from Mars.

1329
02:03:32.125 --> 02:03:33.541
Where is Nanhe?

1330
02:03:33.625 --> 02:03:35.833
It's closed since last night,
he hasn't come.

1331
02:03:35.916 --> 02:03:36.958
Is it?

1332
02:03:37.333 --> 02:03:39.208
If he comes,
tell him Bilkis was here...

1333
02:03:39.291 --> 02:03:40.666
- Okay.
- To give the payment.

1334
02:03:40.750 --> 02:03:41.833
Okay.
